{"parentUuid":"3a3ff5f4-fa66-413f-8281-cbbf052d9510","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EcgRprfQAupvyepQNfKaAL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XFg1KvDAu2ZAUwb8aFYHai","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore aws-lc-sys vulnerability fixes","prompt":"I need to understand how to fix Dependabot security alerts for aws-lc-sys in the Neumann project. The alerts are:\n- PKCS7_verify Certificate Chain Validation Bypass (alerts #19, #20)\n- Timing Side-Channel in AES-CCM Tag Verification (alerts #21, #22)\n- PKCS7_verify Signature Validation Bypass (alerts #23, #24)\n\nThese affect both Cargo.lock and neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock.\n\n1. Check the current aws-lc-sys version in Cargo.lock: grep -A2 'name = \"aws-lc-sys\"' Cargo.lock\n2. Check the same in neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock\n3. Check what depends on aws-lc-sys: look for rustls, ring, or aws-lc-rs in Cargo.toml files\n4. Check if there's a patched version of aws-lc-sys that fixes these CVEs by searching for the latest version available\n5. Check if simply running `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` would fix it\n\nReport what version we're on, what version we need, and whether a simple cargo update fixes it or if we need dependency changes.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2590,"cache_read_input_tokens":140707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2590},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CYz5wttSKpAcMX5r9kahf","type":"assistant","uuid":"c87cafbf-5ea2-4dce-bb73-18961e3816de","timestamp":"2026-03-12T23:53:12.051Z"}
