{"parentUuid":"502fd608-1cd2-46fe-9f72-1318c6180fd6","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-12T23:54:45.296Z","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01X8tQ1a6gD4zyL2QTepQCUq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013QZJwCPpxTuUg9civ3PaBA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr diff 42 --repo Shadylukin/Neumann 2>&1 | head -150"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":876,"cache_read_input_tokens":107226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":876,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz65oNXMnoqwayQYL7k7","uuid":"2bd170bf-66bf-4560-8a8d-3f2caf6b0002"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"a0944e019bb88b7c8"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_01EcgRprfQAupvyepQNfKaAL","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01HzFCXGiYN8Ncit5b2yYSgo","uuid":"083a73d9-ecad-470a-a1bb-0f2d7bf47d7c","timestamp":"2026-03-12T23:54:45.296Z"}
{"parentUuid":"083a73d9-ecad-470a-a1bb-0f2d7bf47d7c","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"type":"hook_progress","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","hookName":"PostToolUse:Agent","command":"entire hooks claude-code post-task"},"parentToolUseID":"toolu_01XFg1KvDAu2ZAUwb8aFYHai","toolUseID":"toolu_01XFg1KvDAu2ZAUwb8aFYHai","timestamp":"2026-03-12T23:54:36.276Z","uuid":"8c042216-69dd-4764-8430-09e875b909e8"}
{"parentUuid":"c87cafbf-5ea2-4dce-bb73-18961e3816de","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XFg1KvDAu2ZAUwb8aFYHai","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have enough information to provide a comprehensive report. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Summary: Dependabot Security Alerts for aws-lc-sys\n\nBased on my analysis of the Neumann project, here's what I found:\n\n### Current Versions\n\n**Main Workspace (Cargo.lock)**\n- `aws-lc-sys`: **0.37.1**\n- `aws-lc-rs`: 1.16.0\n- `rustls`: 0.23.36\n- `ring`: 0.17.14\n- `tonic`: 0.14.4 (with `tls-ring` feature)\n\n**neumann-py/neumann-native (Cargo.lock)**\n- `aws-lc-sys`: **0.37.0** (one version behind main)\n- Depends on same transitive: `query_router`, `relational_engine`, `tensor_store`, `tensor_unified`, `tensor_compress`\n\n### Dependency Chain\n\nThe vulnerable `aws-lc-sys` reaches your code through:\n```\ntonic (0.14) -> rustls (0.23.36) -> aws-lc-rs (1.16.0) -> aws-lc-sys (0.37.1/0.37.0)\n```\n\nAll three CVEs you mentioned (PKCS7_verify bypass variants and AES-CCM timing side-channel) are in the underlying AWS libcrypto library that aws-lc-sys binds to.\n\n### Fix Assessment\n\n**The good news:** aws-lc-sys has releases that patch these CVEs:\n- **aws-lc-sys 0.38.x and later** include patches for these CVEs\n- **Rustls 0.23.x and later** should support newer aws-lc-sys versions\n- **Simple `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` will likely NOT work** because your Cargo.toml doesn't directly depend on aws-lc-sys\n\n### Recommended Fix Strategy\n\n1. **Primary approach**: Update rustls in Cargo.toml\n   - Change `tonic = { version = \"0.14\", features = [\"gzip\", \"tls-ring\"] }` to use rustls with explicit patched aws-lc-sys\n   - Or: add a `[patch.crates-io]` section in Cargo.toml to force aws-lc-sys to a patched version\n\n2. **Secondary approach**: Upgrade tonic to 0.15+ (if available) which may bring updated dependencies\n\n3. **Sync neumann-py**: After fixing the main workspace, regenerate neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock to match\n\n### What Blocks Simple Update\n\nSince `tonic` depends on `rustls` which depends on `aws-lc-rs` which depends on `aws-lc-sys`, you can't just run `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` without updating the upstream packages. Tonic and rustls versions must be compatible with the aws-lc-sys versions they support.\n\n### Files Affected\n\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/Cargo.lock` - main workspace lock\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock` - Python bindings lock\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/Cargo.toml` - main manifest (may need patch or version updates)\n\n### Next Steps\n\n1. Check the latest versions of `rustls` and `tonic` to see if they're compatible\n2. Either bump tonic/rustls versions OR add a `[patch.crates-io]` override for aws-lc-sys\n3. Run `cargo update` to regenerate both lock files\n4. Verify all tests pass and coverage requirements are met\n\nWould you like me to check which specific versions of rustls and tonic support the patched aws-lc-sys (0.38+)?"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a62fd5b7f554128a3 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 92099\ntool_uses: 34\nduration_ms: 74848</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"a9f434c1-72a8-4359-8dec-b44db828340a","timestamp":"2026-03-12T23:54:36.276Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand how to fix Dependabot security alerts for aws-lc-sys in the Neumann project. The alerts are:\n- PKCS7_verify Certificate Chain Validation Bypass (alerts #19, #20)\n- Timing Side-Channel in AES-CCM Tag Verification (alerts #21, #22)\n- PKCS7_verify Signature Validation Bypass (alerts #23, #24)\n\nThese affect both Cargo.lock and neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock.\n\n1. Check the current aws-lc-sys version in Cargo.lock: grep -A2 'name = \"aws-lc-sys\"' Cargo.lock\n2. Check the same in neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock\n3. Check what depends on aws-lc-sys: look for rustls, ring, or aws-lc-rs in Cargo.toml files\n4. Check if there's a patched version of aws-lc-sys that fixes these CVEs by searching for the latest version available\n5. Check if simply running `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` would fix it\n\nReport what version we're on, what version we need, and whether a simple cargo update fixes it or if we need dependency changes.","agentId":"a62fd5b7f554128a3","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have enough information to provide a comprehensive report. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Summary: Dependabot Security Alerts for aws-lc-sys\n\nBased on my analysis of the Neumann project, here's what I found:\n\n### Current Versions\n\n**Main Workspace (Cargo.lock)**\n- `aws-lc-sys`: **0.37.1**\n- `aws-lc-rs`: 1.16.0\n- `rustls`: 0.23.36\n- `ring`: 0.17.14\n- `tonic`: 0.14.4 (with `tls-ring` feature)\n\n**neumann-py/neumann-native (Cargo.lock)**\n- `aws-lc-sys`: **0.37.0** (one version behind main)\n- Depends on same transitive: `query_router`, `relational_engine`, `tensor_store`, `tensor_unified`, `tensor_compress`\n\n### Dependency Chain\n\nThe vulnerable `aws-lc-sys` reaches your code through:\n```\ntonic (0.14) -> rustls (0.23.36) -> aws-lc-rs (1.16.0) -> aws-lc-sys (0.37.1/0.37.0)\n```\n\nAll three CVEs you mentioned (PKCS7_verify bypass variants and AES-CCM timing side-channel) are in the underlying AWS libcrypto library that aws-lc-sys binds to.\n\n### Fix Assessment\n\n**The good news:** aws-lc-sys has releases that patch these CVEs:\n- **aws-lc-sys 0.38.x and later** include patches for these CVEs\n- **Rustls 0.23.x and later** should support newer aws-lc-sys versions\n- **Simple `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` will likely NOT work** because your Cargo.toml doesn't directly depend on aws-lc-sys\n\n### Recommended Fix Strategy\n\n1. **Primary approach**: Update rustls in Cargo.toml\n   - Change `tonic = { version = \"0.14\", features = [\"gzip\", \"tls-ring\"] }` to use rustls with explicit patched aws-lc-sys\n   - Or: add a `[patch.crates-io]` section in Cargo.toml to force aws-lc-sys to a patched version\n\n2. **Secondary approach**: Upgrade tonic to 0.15+ (if available) which may bring updated dependencies\n\n3. **Sync neumann-py**: After fixing the main workspace, regenerate neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock to match\n\n### What Blocks Simple Update\n\nSince `tonic` depends on `rustls` which depends on `aws-lc-rs` which depends on `aws-lc-sys`, you can't just run `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` without updating the upstream packages. Tonic and rustls versions must be compatible with the aws-lc-sys versions they support.\n\n### Files Affected\n\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/Cargo.lock` - main workspace lock\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock` - Python bindings lock\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/Cargo.toml` - main manifest (may need patch or version updates)\n\n### Next Steps\n\n1. Check the latest versions of `rustls` and `tonic` to see if they're compatible\n2. Either bump tonic/rustls versions OR add a `[patch.crates-io]` override for aws-lc-sys\n3. Run `cargo update` to regenerate both lock files\n4. Verify all tests pass and coverage requirements are met\n\nWould you like me to check which specific versions of rustls and tonic support the patched aws-lc-sys (0.38+)?"}],"totalDurationMs":74848,"totalTokens":92099,"totalToolUseCount":34,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":585,"cache_read_input_tokens":90594,"output_tokens":920,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":585},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c87cafbf-5ea2-4dce-bb73-18961e3816de"}
