{"parentUuid":"f5d95785-efd4-4089-918a-cb7264e5692d","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"type":"hook_progress","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","hookName":"PostToolUse:Agent","command":"entire hooks claude-code post-task"},"parentToolUseID":"toolu_01HzFCXGiYN8Ncit5b2yYSgo","toolUseID":"toolu_01HzFCXGiYN8Ncit5b2yYSgo","timestamp":"2026-03-12T23:55:04.866Z","uuid":"619c14e9-8e16-4c88-97ba-e671329764f5"}
{"parentUuid":"f9323360-0b68-4dbb-94e3-60440ca3b0ff","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HzFCXGiYN8Ncit5b2yYSgo","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! So PR #43 only changes the Cargo.toml version. Now I have all the information I need. Let me provide a comprehensive report.\n\n## CI Status Report for PRs #42 and #43\n\n### PR #42 (criterion 0.5.1 → 0.8.2)\n\n**CI Check Status:**\n- **Pass:** Clippy, Format, Benchmark Inventory, Cargo Deny, CodeQL, Coverage, Cross-Platform (macOS, Ubuntu, Windows), Doc Coverage, Documentation, Miri, Publish Dry Run, Security Audit, Stress Tests, Test suite\n- **Fail:** Docker Build & Scan (vulnerability scan step), CI Success summary\n- **Skip:** Python SDK, TypeScript SDK\n\n**Findings:**\nThe Docker vulnerability scan failure is an **infrastructure/CI issue**, not a code issue. The actual Docker image builds pass (`Build CLI image` and `Build Server image` both succeed), but the Trivy vulnerability scanning step fails. This appears to affect both PRs equally.\n\n**Code Changes Needed:** **NONE**\n- Criterion 0.5.1 → 0.8.2 is backward compatible for the benchmark API used in this codebase\n- All benchmark files use standard criterion features that didn't change:\n  - `criterion_group!()` macro\n  - `criterion_main!()` macro\n  - `BenchmarkId::new()` and `BenchmarkId::from_parameter()`\n  - `Throughput::Bytes()` and `Throughput::Elements()`\n  - `bench_with_input()`, `bench_function()`\n  - `group.finish()`\n- The new criterion 0.8 MSRV is 1.86 (project targets 1.75 but should be compatible)\n- Dropped async-std support doesn't affect the code (not used in benchmarks)\n\n---\n\n### PR #43 (tabled 0.17 → 0.20)\n\n**CI Check Status:**\n- **Pass:** Clippy, Format, Benchmark Inventory, Cargo Deny, CodeQL, Coverage, Cross-Platform (macOS, Ubuntu, Windows), Doc Coverage, Documentation, Miri, Publish Dry Run, Security Audit, Stress Tests, Test suite\n- **Fail:** Docker Build & Scan (vulnerability scan step), CI Success summary\n- **Skip:** Python SDK, TypeScript SDK\n\n**Findings:**\nSame Docker vulnerability scan infrastructure failure. The actual code builds and tests pass.\n\n**Code Changes Needed:** **MINIMAL BUT IMPORTANT**\n\nBased on tabled 0.17 → 0.20 changelog, two breaking API changes apply to `neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs`:\n\n1. **`Columns::single` → `Columns::one`** and **`Rows::single` → `Rows::one`**\n   - In tabled 0.20, these were renamed for consistency\n   - Current code doesn't appear to use these directly (uses `Rows::first()` instead)\n\n2. **`with(Border)` behavior changed** - now sets only outer border instead of all cell borders\n   - Current code in table.rs uses `Style::rounded()` which should be unaffected\n   - But if any code uses `Border` directly, it will behave differently\n\n3. **`Table::from_iter()` still exists** - confirmed available in 0.20 (used in table.rs line 60)\n\n**Actual Code Changes Needed in `neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs`:**\n- Line 62: `Rows::first()` may need to change to `Rows::one()` if it still exists in 0.20\n- OR investigate whether `Rows::first()` is still the correct way to target the first row\n\nLet me check the actual current usage:\n\nThe file uses:\n```rust\n.with(Modify::new(Rows::first()).with(Alignment::center()))\n```\n\nThis likely needs updating to the new tabled 0.20 API. You should check if `Rows::first()` exists in 0.20 or if it needs to be `Rows::one()` or another method.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n**Both PRs fail for the same reason:** Docker vulnerability scanning (Trivy) infrastructure issue, not code-related.\n\n**PR #42 (criterion):** ✅ No code changes needed - backward compatible API\n\n**PR #43 (tabled):** ⚠️ **Requires code changes in neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs:**\n- Check tabled 0.20 documentation for the correct way to reference the first row (likely `Rows::one()` instead of `Rows::first()`)\n- Verify `Table::from_iter()` still works or if the construction method changed\n- Test that `Style::rounded()` still produces rounded borders\n\nThe Docker failure is blocking both PRs from showing \"CI Success\" but is unrelated to the dependency upgrades themselves."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a0944e019bb88b7c8 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 114399\ntool_uses: 31\nduration_ms: 108097</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"37d7abd5-6eac-400d-aaed-93c2ffdb4650","timestamp":"2026-03-12T23:55:04.865Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Check the CI status for PRs #42 and #43 on the Shadylukin/Neumann repo. For each:\n1. Run: gh pr checks 42 --repo Shadylukin/Neumann 2>&1\n2. Run: gh pr checks 43 --repo Shadylukin/Neumann 2>&1\n3. If there are failures, check the failure details - especially Clippy and build failures\n4. For #42 (criterion 0.5 → 0.8), check what criterion API changes are needed by looking at the bench files\n5. For #43 (tabled 0.17 → 0.20), check what tabled API is used in neumann_shell\n\nReport: which CI checks pass/fail, what code changes would be needed for each PR to work.","agentId":"a0944e019bb88b7c8","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! So PR #43 only changes the Cargo.toml version. Now I have all the information I need. Let me provide a comprehensive report.\n\n## CI Status Report for PRs #42 and #43\n\n### PR #42 (criterion 0.5.1 → 0.8.2)\n\n**CI Check Status:**\n- **Pass:** Clippy, Format, Benchmark Inventory, Cargo Deny, CodeQL, Coverage, Cross-Platform (macOS, Ubuntu, Windows), Doc Coverage, Documentation, Miri, Publish Dry Run, Security Audit, Stress Tests, Test suite\n- **Fail:** Docker Build & Scan (vulnerability scan step), CI Success summary\n- **Skip:** Python SDK, TypeScript SDK\n\n**Findings:**\nThe Docker vulnerability scan failure is an **infrastructure/CI issue**, not a code issue. The actual Docker image builds pass (`Build CLI image` and `Build Server image` both succeed), but the Trivy vulnerability scanning step fails. This appears to affect both PRs equally.\n\n**Code Changes Needed:** **NONE**\n- Criterion 0.5.1 → 0.8.2 is backward compatible for the benchmark API used in this codebase\n- All benchmark files use standard criterion features that didn't change:\n  - `criterion_group!()` macro\n  - `criterion_main!()` macro\n  - `BenchmarkId::new()` and `BenchmarkId::from_parameter()`\n  - `Throughput::Bytes()` and `Throughput::Elements()`\n  - `bench_with_input()`, `bench_function()`\n  - `group.finish()`\n- The new criterion 0.8 MSRV is 1.86 (project targets 1.75 but should be compatible)\n- Dropped async-std support doesn't affect the code (not used in benchmarks)\n\n---\n\n### PR #43 (tabled 0.17 → 0.20)\n\n**CI Check Status:**\n- **Pass:** Clippy, Format, Benchmark Inventory, Cargo Deny, CodeQL, Coverage, Cross-Platform (macOS, Ubuntu, Windows), Doc Coverage, Documentation, Miri, Publish Dry Run, Security Audit, Stress Tests, Test suite\n- **Fail:** Docker Build & Scan (vulnerability scan step), CI Success summary\n- **Skip:** Python SDK, TypeScript SDK\n\n**Findings:**\nSame Docker vulnerability scan infrastructure failure. The actual code builds and tests pass.\n\n**Code Changes Needed:** **MINIMAL BUT IMPORTANT**\n\nBased on tabled 0.17 → 0.20 changelog, two breaking API changes apply to `neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs`:\n\n1. **`Columns::single` → `Columns::one`** and **`Rows::single` → `Rows::one`**\n   - In tabled 0.20, these were renamed for consistency\n   - Current code doesn't appear to use these directly (uses `Rows::first()` instead)\n\n2. **`with(Border)` behavior changed** - now sets only outer border instead of all cell borders\n   - Current code in table.rs uses `Style::rounded()` which should be unaffected\n   - But if any code uses `Border` directly, it will behave differently\n\n3. **`Table::from_iter()` still exists** - confirmed available in 0.20 (used in table.rs line 60)\n\n**Actual Code Changes Needed in `neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs`:**\n- Line 62: `Rows::first()` may need to change to `Rows::one()` if it still exists in 0.20\n- OR investigate whether `Rows::first()` is still the correct way to target the first row\n\nLet me check the actual current usage:\n\nThe file uses:\n```rust\n.with(Modify::new(Rows::first()).with(Alignment::center()))\n```\n\nThis likely needs updating to the new tabled 0.20 API. You should check if `Rows::first()` exists in 0.20 or if it needs to be `Rows::one()` or another method.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n**Both PRs fail for the same reason:** Docker vulnerability scanning (Trivy) infrastructure issue, not code-related.\n\n**PR #42 (criterion):** ✅ No code changes needed - backward compatible API\n\n**PR #43 (tabled):** ⚠️ **Requires code changes in neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs:**\n- Check tabled 0.20 documentation for the correct way to reference the first row (likely `Rows::one()` instead of `Rows::first()`)\n- Verify `Table::from_iter()` still works or if the construction method changed\n- Test that `Style::rounded()` still produces rounded borders\n\nThe Docker failure is blocking both PRs from showing \"CI Success\" but is unrelated to the dependency upgrades themselves."}],"totalDurationMs":108097,"totalTokens":114399,"totalToolUseCount":31,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":377,"cache_read_input_tokens":112861,"output_tokens":1161,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":377},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f9323360-0b68-4dbb-94e3-60440ca3b0ff"}
