{"parentUuid":"212e8f31-a687-4826-8a44-e55e3b96cd27","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to plan fixes for the remaining items in the Neumann project. Here's the context:\n\n## Remaining PRs\n1. **PR #42 (criterion 0.5 → 0.8)**: CI passes (except Docker vulnerability scan, which is infrastructure). No code changes needed — API is backward compatible. The only concern is MSRV (criterion 0.8 needs Rust 1.86, project says rust-version = \"1.75\").\n2. **PR #43 (tabled 0.17 → 0.20)**: CI passes (same Docker scan issue). May need code changes in neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs. Uses `Rows::first()`, `Style::rounded()`, `Table::from_iter()`.\n\n## Security Alerts (6 alerts, 3 CVEs across 2 lock files)\n### aws-lc-sys vulnerabilities (alerts #19-24):\n- Current: aws-lc-sys 0.37.1 in Cargo.lock, 0.37.0 in neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock\n- Fix needed: aws-lc-sys >= 0.38.0 (patches PKCS7_verify bypass and AES-CCM timing side-channel)\n- Dependency chain: tonic → rustls → aws-lc-rs → aws-lc-sys\n- Need to check if `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` suffices or if upstream deps need bumping\n\n### minimatch ReDoS (alert #26):\n- Vulnerable minimatch 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 in neumann-ts/package-lock.json\n- Fix: need minimatch >= 10.0.1\n- eslint and @typescript-eslint packages depend on it\n- PR #57 (eslint v10) was already merged, PR #55 (@typescript-eslint/parser 8.56.1) was merged — these may have partially fixed it\n\n## Key Questions to Address in Plan:\n1. Can we merge PR #42 given the MSRV concern (criterion 0.8 requires Rust 1.86 but we declare 1.75)?\n2. For PR #43, what exact code changes are needed in table.rs?\n3. For aws-lc-sys: can `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` get us to 0.38+, or do we need to bump tonic/rustls?\n4. For minimatch: after merging PRs #55 and #57, is the vulnerability resolved or do we need more npm updates?\n\nPlease design a concrete implementation plan for addressing all of these."}]},"uuid":"3425699f-b67b-4f66-9f9a-1286f5fd5be1","timestamp":"2026-03-12T23:57:53.303Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"I need to plan fixes for the remaining items in the Neumann project. Here's the context:\n\n## Remaining PRs\n1. **PR #42 (criterion 0.5 → 0.8)**: CI passes (except Docker vulnerability scan, which is infrastructure). No code changes needed — API is backward compatible. The only concern is MSRV (criterion 0.8 needs Rust 1.86, project says rust-version = \"1.75\").\n2. **PR #43 (tabled 0.17 → 0.20)**: CI passes (same Docker scan issue). May need code changes in neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs. Uses `Rows::first()`, `Style::rounded()`, `Table::from_iter()`.\n\n## Security Alerts (6 alerts, 3 CVEs across 2 lock files)\n### aws-lc-sys vulnerabilities (alerts #19-24):\n- Current: aws-lc-sys 0.37.1 in Cargo.lock, 0.37.0 in neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock\n- Fix needed: aws-lc-sys >= 0.38.0 (patches PKCS7_verify bypass and AES-CCM timing side-channel)\n- Dependency chain: tonic → rustls → aws-lc-rs → aws-lc-sys\n- Need to check if `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` suffices or if upstream deps need bumping\n\n### minimatch ReDoS (alert #26):\n- Vulnerable minimatch 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 in neumann-ts/package-lock.json\n- Fix: need minimatch >= 10.0.1\n- eslint and @typescript-eslint packages depend on it\n- PR #57 (eslint v10) was already merged, PR #55 (@typescript-eslint/parser 8.56.1) was merged — these may have partially fixed it\n\n## Key Questions to Address in Plan:\n1. Can we merge PR #42 given the MSRV concern (criterion 0.8 requires Rust 1.86 but we declare 1.75)?\n2. For PR #43, what exact code changes are needed in table.rs?\n3. For aws-lc-sys: can `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` get us to 0.38+, or do we need to bump tonic/rustls?\n4. For minimatch: after merging PRs #55 and #57, is the vulnerability resolved or do we need more npm updates?\n\nPlease design a concrete implementation plan for addressing all of these.","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"18e93e99-86e9-45e9-9f67-30f5e1aedbf7","timestamp":"2026-03-12T23:57:53.304Z"}
