{"parentUuid":"958dcee9-744e-43cb-b366-b48d2827e414","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:20.307Z","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012jZFoWUzoTvaeean3qMmjt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0142rtY4mTvAYmhwz3sJDShM","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.rs/tabled/0.20.0/tabled/","prompt":"Does tabled 0.20 still have Table::from_iter? Does it still have settings::Style::rounded(), settings::object::Rows::first(), settings::Alignment::center(), and settings::Modify? Show the module structure and any changes from older versions."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":889,"cache_read_input_tokens":36595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":889,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz6WAbPnpa5D2nyb4zHN","uuid":"670f757c-c08c-4c99-a3bb-f70ea396be9e"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"311b1309-5785-4adc-861c-a57389fdc39b","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:20.311Z"}
{"parentUuid":"311b1309-5785-4adc-861c-a57389fdc39b","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0142rtY4mTvAYmhwz3sJDShM","type":"tool_result","content":"# Tabled 0.20.0 API Analysis\n\nBased on the documentation provided, I cannot definitively confirm whether `Table::from_iter`, `settings::Style::rounded()`, `settings::object::Rows::first()`, `settings::Alignment::center()`, and `settings::Modify` exist in version 0.20.0, as the page doesn't list these specific methods.\n\n## What the Documentation Shows\n\nThe page confirms these **do exist**:\n\n- **`Table`** type with constructor `Table::new()`\n- **`settings` module** containing configuration options\n- **`Style`** with at least a `modern()` variant (demonstrated in examples)\n- **`Alignment`** trait (used with `Alignment::right()` in examples)\n- **`Modify`** functionality (referenced as `table.modify()` method)\n- **`Builder`** for dynamic table construction\n\n## Module Structure\n\nThe crate organizes functionality into these modules:\n\n- `tables` - Table implementations\n- `settings` - Configuration and styling\n- `builder` - Dynamic table construction\n- `derive` - Macro support\n- `grid` - Underlying grid system\n- `iter` - Iterator utilities\n- `assert` - Testing helpers\n\nThe documentation lacks comprehensive API reference details for older version comparisons or complete method listings, so checking the GitHub repository or crates.io directly would provide definitive answers about specific method availability."}]},"uuid":"b50f87ec-f194-4b09-bc95-8cbf0f4c8e00","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:25.544Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","par