{"parentUuid":"b298d88f-0161-42ad-b7de-002d65ecb89c","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:30.293Z","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VcEmjh2pbFHTfevdNuVsiB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KgkY4kcALwcTwQLmcH3XRK","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.rs/tabled/0.20.0/tabled/struct.Table.html","prompt":"Does Table implement FromIterator? Does it have a from_iter method? List all creation/construction methods."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":974,"cache_read_input_tokens":37484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":974,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz6X41YFLD9Ey4oK7iE9","uuid":"eee70f40-bc02-4944-9576-4c50bb78feea"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"e0a0284d-4f5e-44be-81e0-2f2f24a2bc33","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:30.294Z"}
{"parentUuid":"e0a0284d-4f5e-44be-81e0-2f2f24a2bc33","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Request failed with status code 404","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KgkY4kcALwcTwQLmcH3XRK"}]},"uuid":"be8a0f82-7b07-480b-b34f-df04da8ae43b","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:30.670Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Request failed with status code 404"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"d4f5adbd-f77c-48c0-b1b6-9508ecba79a3","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:30.671Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d4f5adbd-f77c-48c0-b1b6-9508ecba79a3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WUspsLNuvZxMa96Cg51s8i","type":"tool_result","content":"# Rows Methods\n\nYes, `Rows` has a `first()` method. According to the documentation, it \"Returns a first row [`Object`](trait.Object.html). If the table has 0 rows returns an empty set of cells.\"\n\n## All Available Methods on Rows\n\nThe `Rows` struct provides the following methods:\n\n1. **`new(range: R)`** - Creates a new instance for a range of rows, where R implements `RangeBounds<usize>`\n\n2. **`one(index: usize)`** - Returns a new instance with a single row at the specified index\n\n3. **`first()`** - Returns the first row as an Object; returns an empty set if the table has no rows\n\n4. **`last()`** - Returns the last row as an Object; returns an empty set if the table has no rows\n\nAdditionally, through trait implementations, `Rows` inherits methods like `and()`, `not()`, `intersect()`, `inverse()`, `skip()`, `step_by()`, and `filter()` from the `Object` and `ObjectIterator` traits."}]},"uuid":"e1b9a6fe-5859-4635-aead-756f1b310660","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:33.634Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"ee2a18e4-d673-4c4a-bcb8-4e2f6d7c89a1","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:33.635Z"}
{"parentUuid":"ee2a18e4-d673-4c4a-bcb8-4e2f6d7c89a1","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PQv5v1EcWMPWapn5cNjMoh","type":"tool_result","content":"# Style Methods and Constants\n\nYes, `Style` has a `rounded()` method. Here are the available style methods/constants:\n\n## Preset Styles\n- `empty()` - No styling options\n- `blank()` - Empty with vertical space separator\n- `ascii()` - ASCII charset with horizontal/vertical lines\n- `ascii_rounded()` - ASCII with rounded corners, no horizontals\n- `psql()` - PostgreSQL-like style\n- `markdown()` - Markdown table format\n- `modern()` - UTF-8 with vertical/horizontal splits\n- `sharp()` - Modern without horizontal lines except header\n- `rounded()` - Sharp style with rounded corners\n- `modern_rounded()` - Rounded with horizontal lines\n- `extended()` - Double-line UTF-8 style\n- `dots()` - Dots and colons only\n- `re_structured_text()` - ReStructuredText format\n\n## Customization Methods\n- `top(char)` - Set top border\n- `bottom(char)` - Set bottom border\n- `left(char)` - Set left border\n- `right(char)` - Set right border\n- `horizontal(char)` - Set horizontal split line\n- `vertical(char)` - Set vertical split line\n- `corner_top_left(char)`, `corner_top_right(char)`, `corner_bottom_left(char)`, `corner_bottom_right(char)`\n- `intersection(char)`, `intersection_top(char)`, `intersection_bottom(char)`, `intersection_left(char)`, `intersection_right(char)`\n- `horizontals()` - Set custom horizontal lines\n- `verticals()` - Set custom vertical lines\n- `remove_*()` variants for removing borders/lines"}]},"uuid":"1ba8de7f-a2c0-450f-a1ff-f1ee1b0354bc","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:33.993Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"98556da3-ecd6-41a5-be3b-5a5bdf14415e","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:33.995Z"}
