{"parentUuid":"63b7146b-c130-4bc5-a8c0-f2fe29dec8d0","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:46.502Z","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017ZrqfdyftUyvRXWBiUFK4f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TJRVpwY3a2QrLKdCieK4b8","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.rs/tabled/0.20.0/tabled/settings/struct.Modify.html","prompt":"Does Modify exist in tabled 0.20? What is its API? How is it used with Rows and Alignment?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":314,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":38458,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":776,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz6XgDPqvjeQF7zvvEme","uuid":"acec2fd4-4373-4556-8426-69287792cc4b"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"da7b2258-6bdb-4aea-bcb2-88666222d017","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:46.502Z"}
{"parentUuid":"da7b2258-6bdb-4aea-bcb2-88666222d017","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014zw9VJkX1HMEH4KzHdxCEV","type":"tool_result","content":"# Table's FromIterator Implementation and Construction Methods\n\n## FromIterator Implementation\n\nYes, `Table` implements `FromIterator`. The documentation states:\n\n> \"impl<T> FromIterator<T> for Table where T: IntoIterator, T::Item: Into<String>\"\n\nThis trait is implemented directly on the struct.\n\n## Creation/Construction Methods\n\nThe `Table` struct provides several primary construction methods:\n\n1. **`Table::new(iter)`** - Creates a table from an iterator of `Tabled` values with a header row\n2. **`Table::with_capacity(iter, count_rows)`** - Optimized version of `new()` when row count is known\n3. **`Table::nohead(iter)`** - Creates a table without a header from `Tabled` values\n4. **`Table::kv(iter)`** - Creates a key-value style table layout\n5. **`Table::builder(iter)`** - Returns a `Builder` for more customized table construction\n6. **`Table::from_iter(iter)`** - Uses the `FromIterator` trait implementation\n\n## Relevant Trait Implementations\n\n- `Clone`\n- `Debug`\n- `Default`\n- `Display`\n- `FromIterator<T>`\n- `From<Builder>` and `From<Table>` for type conversion\n- `PartialEq` and `Eq`\n- Standard traits: `Send`, `Sync`, `Unpin`, `UnwindSafe`"}]},"uuid":"1a5943e1-eb6e-4a0e-a0e9-52b48c300c2e","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:51.182Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"6f6c3983-9cd3-4707-b72d-2e374f822434","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:51.183Z"}
{"parentUuid":"6f6c3983-9cd3-4707-b72d-2e374f822434","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TJRVpwY3a2QrLKdCieK4b8","type":"tool_result","content":"# Modify in Tabled 0.20.0\n\nYes, `Modify` exists in tabled 0.20.0. Here's what the documentation reveals:\n\n## Core Purpose\n`Modify` is a generic struct that provides \"an abstraction, to be able to apply a set of `CellOption`s to the same object.\" It allows chainable configuration of table cell formatting.\n\n## Key API Methods\n\n- **`new(obj: O)`**: Creates a new `Modify` instance without options\n- **`with<M>(self, next: M)`**: Stores a `CellOption` in a builder pattern, returning a `ModifyList`\n- **`list<M>(obj: O, next: M)`**: Combines `new()` and `with()` into one call\n\n## Usage with Rows and Alignment\n\nThe documentation provides this example:\n\n```rust\nTable::new(&[\"Year\", \"2021\"])\n    .with(Modify::list(Rows::first(), Alignment::center()))\n```\n\nThis demonstrates that `Modify` accepts a row selector (`Rows::first()`) and a formatting option (`Alignment::center()`), applying the alignment to cells in the first row.\n\nThe pattern chains modifications: create a `Modify`, specify the target cells/rows, then apply formatting options via `.with()`."}]},"uuid":"1240d789-51a5-4a65-85cc-4972589b2e56","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:51.815Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"8bcc584e-5715-4cd3-9791-56450400f3f5","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:51.816Z"}
{"parentUuid":"8bcc584e-5715-4cd3-9791-56450400f3f5","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:59.834Z","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01V1Hnt9Fw6KJMTuSzk26t9y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016xxmpEyLHdXYZrjeSnNsgy","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.rs/tabled/0.17.0/tabled/settings/struct.Modify.html","prompt":"Show the Modify API in tabled 0.17. What methods does it have? How is it used?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1525,"cache_read_input_tokens":39234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1525,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz6YzM5QcrFzzhBEGCsd","uuid":"0ac7eb6c-e41a-4729-8207-857f4056e4ed"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"54258586-922b-4ed9-9c9e-b4bd195b5fdb","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:00:59.835Z"}
{"parentUuid":"54258586-922b-4ed9-9c9e-b4bd195b5fdb","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:00.519Z","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01V1Hnt9Fw6KJMTuSzk26t9y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KxT2cws3GmcEKhbDjNnQbe","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.rs/tabled/0.20.0/tabled/settings/struct.Alignment.html","prompt":"Show the Alignment API. Does Alignment::center() still exist? How is it used?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1525,"cache_read_input_tokens":39234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1525,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz6YzM5QcrFzzhBEGCsd","uuid":"711737af-fcb6-4704-a6bc-66f68a20fe65"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"6f4600e9-5967-40e0-9a54-74b0f9b37b7c","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:00.519Z"}
{"parentUuid":"6f4600e9-5967-40e0-9a54-74b0f9b37b7c","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KxT2cws3GmcEKhbDjNnQbe","type":"tool_result","content":"# Alignment API in tabled\n\nYes, `Alignment::center()` still exists. According to the documentation, it is described as:\n\n> \"Center constructs a horizontal alignment to `AlignmentHorizontal::Center`\"\n\n## Usage\n\n`Alignment::center()` is used as a table setting to horizontally center-align cell content. It's typically applied using the `.with()` method:\n\n```rust\ntable.with(Alignment::center());\n```\n\nOr more granularly with `Modify`:\n\n```rust\n.modify(Rows::first(), Alignment::center())\n```\n\nThe documentation shows it implements both `CellOption` and `TableOption` traits, allowing it to be applied to entire tables or specific cells. The API also supports combining horizontal and vertical alignment in a single `Alignment` struct, with related methods like `center_vertical()`, `left()`, `right()`, `top()`, and `bottom()`."}]},"uuid":"b8254b47-4f33-4504-81a9-0e7b1d0dae0d","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:04.963Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"c2a831ff-1f5a-4174-a124-a0b4f4657025","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:04.964Z"}
{"parentUuid":"c2a831ff-1f5a-4174-a124-a0b4f4657025","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016xxmpEyLHdXYZrjeSnNsgy","type":"tool_result","content":"# Modify API in tabled 0.17.0\n\n## Overview\nThe `Modify` struct is a generic abstraction that enables applying multiple `CellOption` settings to the same target object. It's available when the `std` feature is enabled.\n\n## Methods\n\n**`new(obj: O)`** - Creates a new `Modify` instance without any options applied.\n\n**`with<M>(self, next: M)`** - A generic function that stores a `CellOption`. This method chains settings together but doesn't modify the table until the `Modify` object is passed to `Table::with()`.\n\n**`list<M>(obj: O, next: M)`** - Combines `new()` and `with()` functionality into a single call for convenience.\n\n## Usage Pattern\n\nThe typical workflow involves:\n1. Creating a `Modify` instance with a target object\n2. Chaining `with()` calls to add multiple settings\n3. Passing the configured `Modify` to `Table::with()`\n\n**Example:**\n```rust\nTable::new(&data)\n    .with(Modify::new(Rows::first()).with(Padding::new(1, 1, 1, 1)))\n```\n\nNote: Settings are applied to an entire cell at once, sometimes requiring multiple separate `Modify` calls to achieve desired effects."}]},"uuid":"dba62e38-da05-49b7-95bd-0d169d956103","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:05.293Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"1ccfe9bd-de60-460c-b4db-4b642df376c0","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:05.294Z"}
{"parentUuid":"1ccfe9bd-de60-460c-b4db-4b642df376c0","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:10.549Z","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HYDiZDemCbCzHd1LBnatYP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01385exYbCvjFtmf8f8o942G","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.rs/tabled/0.20.0/tabled/tables/struct.Table.html","prompt":"Does Table have a .with() method that takes TableOption? Show the signature and how it's used. Also does Table have a .modify() method?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":240,"cache_creation_input_tokens":812,"cache_read_input_tokens":40759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":812,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz6ZyyHZfg5r8NCnmWGB","uuid":"17fb4f24-d06d-4537-8801-b089c602b004"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"002d277b-847f-4df5-b308-48e235c40bea","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:10.550Z"}
{"parentUuid":"002d277b-847f-4df5-b308-48e235c40bea","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01385exYbCvjFtmf8f8o942G","type":"tool_result","content":"# Table Methods: `.with()` and `.modify()`\n\n## `.with()` Method\n\nYes, `Table` has a `.with()` method. Here's the signature:\n\n```rust\npub fn with<O>(&mut self, option: O) -> &mut Self\nwhere O: TableOption<VecRecords<Text<String>>, ColoredConfig, CompleteDimension>\n```\n\n**Usage example:**\n```rust\nlet mut table = Table::new(data);\ntable.with(Style::markdown());\n```\n\nThe method \"applies options to the Table\" and \"applies settings immediately.\"\n\n## `.modify()` Method\n\nYes, `Table` also has a `.modify()` method. Here's the signature:\n\n```rust\npub fn modify<T, O>(&mut self, target: T, option: O) -> &mut Self\nwhere T: Object<VecRecords<Text<String>>>,\n      O: CellOption<VecRecords<Text<String>>, ColoredConfig> + Clone\n```\n\n**Usage example:**\n```rust\nlet mut table = Table::new(data);\ntable.modify(Columns::first(), Alignment::right());\n```\n\nThis method \"applies options to particular cells on the Table\" using target selectors like `Cell`, `Rows`, or `Columns`."}]},"uuid":"82c04211-6a92-442d-bbdf-6260663656ab","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:14.233Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"91ff6e4e-52a2-48a6-adac-bbfbd89e7a69","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:14.234Z"}
{"parentUuid":"91ff6e4e-52a2-48a6-adac-bbfbd89e7a69","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:19.006Z","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VuLZB8ngnTmZTqQ7R7BnY4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B8NfqNLvGjiqunwkLFsLHD","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.rs/tabled/0.20.0/tabled/settings/index.html","prompt":"List all the re-exports and items in the settings module. Does it still re-export Modify, Style, Alignment at this path? Is there a settings::object submodule?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":41571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1046,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz6aeCBSCUK9cfZb4QdX","uuid":"6154e261-ccd6-4847-ace5-45e9dc0a575f"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"6cec4d8e-dae8-4c89-9daf-c02dbfbaaa83","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:19.007Z"}
{"parentUuid":"6cec4d8e-dae8-4c89-9daf-c02dbfbaaa83","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B8NfqNLvGjiqunwkLFsLHD","type":"tool_result","content":"# Settings Module Analysis\n\n## Re-exports\n\nThe module re-exports the following items:\n\n- `Border` (from `style`)\n- `Style` (from `style`)\n- `Remove` (from `disable`)\n- `Format` (from `format`)\n- `Height` (from `height`)\n- `Highlight` (from `highlight`)\n- `Merge` (from `merge`)\n- `Panel` (from `panel`)\n- `Span` (from `span`)\n- `Theme` (from `themes`)\n- `Width` (from `width`)\n\n## Notable Findings\n\n**Modify and Alignment are NOT re-exported** at the `settings::` path level. However, both exist as structs within the module itself—`Modify` appears in the Structs section and `Alignment` is listed separately.\n\n**Style IS re-exported** at `settings::Style`.\n\n**Yes, there is a `settings::object` submodule.** The documentation states it \"contains a list of primitives that implement an `Object` trait\" to help locate segments on a table. However, the actual contents aren't detailed in this excerpt."}]},"uuid":"3ae70bf3-3d79-41ca-8289-6b57b10fb05c","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:22.946Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"03919658-ac71-477b-ad85-108627e7697f","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:22.948Z"}
{"parentUuid":"03919658-ac71-477b-ad85-108627e7697f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:32.644Z","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UqV9NjAk3HYTxCZKXTZt4o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HV52dp3VcNBjRC32LReWoa","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.rs/tabled/0.17.0/tabled/settings/index.html","prompt":"List all the re-exports and items in the settings module of tabled 0.17. Does it re-export Modify and Alignment at this path?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":501,"cache_read_input_tokens":42617,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":501,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz6bHRYkqjzG8EvZAfzR","uuid":"679d17fa-8088-42f9-a697-5d14a3f4e28f"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"869bbacb-d942-49e1-8e88-a979aecea697","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:32.646Z"}
{"parentUuid":"869bbacb-d942-49e1-8e88-a979aecea697","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HV52dp3VcNBjRC32LReWoa","type":"tool_result","content":"# Tabled 0.17.0 Settings Module Re-exports and Items\n\n## Re-exports\n\nThe module re-exports the following items:\n\n- `Border` (from style)\n- `Style` (from style)\n- `Remove` (from disable)\n- `Format` (from format)\n- `Height` (from height)\n- `Highlight` (from highlight)\n- `Merge` (from merge)\n- `Panel` (from panel)\n- `Span` (from span)\n- `Theme` (from themes)\n- `Width` (from width)\n\n## Answer to Your Question\n\n**No**, neither `Modify` nor `Alignment` are re-exported at the settings module path. However, both exist as structs within the module itself:\n\n- `Modify` is described as \"provide an abstraction, to be able to apply a set of CellOptions to the same object\"\n- `Alignment` represents \"a horizontal and vertical alignment setting for any cell\"\n\nSince they appear in the Structs section rather than Re-exports, they're defined directly in `tabled::settings` rather than re-exported from submodules."}]},"uuid":"9e5d1d6e-89f6-45b2-afbf-703fe8b7d548","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:36.684Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"f8a04cd4-1db2-46c6-a4bb-54de9e15fd82","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:36.685Z"}
