{"parentUuid":"181c5b76-677b-4cb2-9c71-3c1d324908c5","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RbWfxP2CX69dV91az977Wn","type":"tool_result","content":"# The `.with()` Method Signature\n\nBased on the documentation, the `.with()` method signature is:\n\n```rust\npub fn with<O>(&mut self, option: O) -> &mut Self\n```\n\n## Answer\n\nThis is a **borrowing method**, not a consuming one. It takes `&mut self` and returns `&mut Self`, allowing you to chain multiple `.with()` calls on the same `Table` instance without transferring ownership. The method applies settings immediately and permits continued mutation of the table."}]},"uuid":"f18a98dc-b66f-444b-9799-16bc4d3ff8bf","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:50.359Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"4e53b301-968a-4c43-81a6-f1bb6e0e23d1","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:01:50.361Z"}
