{"parentUuid":"69e8af5f-055b-4e0f-bf9b-b6067c462216","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P2p6PgXUvmtm4pF8iRHMNj","type":"tool_result","content":"# GitHub Advisory for minimatch ReDoS\n\nBased on the page content provided, there are **5 advisories** for minimatch ReDoS vulnerabilities, all marked as \"High\" severity:\n\n1. **GHSA-7r86-cg39-jmmj** (CVE-2026-27903) - \"matchOne() combinatorial backtracking via multiple non-adjacent GLOBSTAR segments\"\n\n2. **GHSA-23c5-xmqv-rm74** (CVE-2026-27904) - \"nested *() extglobs generate catastrophically backtracking regular expressions\"\n\n3. **GHSA-3ppc-4f35-3m26** (CVE-2026-26996) - \"repeated wildcards with non-matching literal in pattern\"\n\n4. **GHSA-f8q6-p94x-37v3** (CVE-2022-3517)\n\n5. **GHSA-hxm2-r34f-qmc5** (CVE-2016-10540)\n\n## Limitation\n\nThe provided content does **not include specific information** about which versions are affected or what patched versions are available. To get those details, you would need to visit the individual advisory pages on GitHub's Advisory Database, as the excerpt only shows the advisory titles and CVE identifiers."}]},"uuid":"499f303e-d715-4aad-8137-2a0842da1f3e","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:07:29.390Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"c22831ef-66de-4b6b-8181-63d4159b7fd1","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:07:29.390Z"}
{"parentUuid":"c22831ef-66de-4b6b-8181-63d4159b7fd1","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YG2wbMEDUbXWhLeejQcatD","type":"tool_result","content":"# Minimatch Version Information\n\n**Latest Version:** 10.2.4\n\n**Most Recent Versions:**\n- 10.2.4 (latest)\n- 10.2.3\n- 10.2.2\n- 10.2.1\n- 10.2.0\n\n## ReDoS Vulnerability Fix Status\n\nThe data shows that versions 0.0.1 through 3.0.0 carried a deprecation notice: \"Please update to minimatch 3.0.2 or higher to avoid a RegExp DoS issue.\" This indicates **3.0.2 was the first patch addressing the vulnerability**.\n\nHowever, there is no evidence of a 3.1.x patch specifically fixing the ReDoS issue. The 3.1.x line (3.1.0, 3.1.1, 3.1.2) came after the fix but appears to be maintained as a legacy branch. The major version bump to 4.0.0 and subsequent releases (5.x, 6.x through 10.x) represent the primary evolution of the library with the vulnerability resolved.\n\n**Recommendation:** While 3.0.2+ technically contains the fix, users should prefer version 10.2.4 or other recent releases for current dependency management."}]},"uuid":"7580d183-8a29-45bf-b331-c9839b6e3fd3","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:07:29.473Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"2ab342b0-ded1-4f29-ae23-b0d74277c9e2","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:07:29.473Z"}
