{"parentUuid":"670344ae-aedd-4787-b19c-752a38b3ca5d","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K1nfRjyAh2E9YUUjEqbxiD","type":"tool_result","content":"# Criterion 0.8.2 Features\n\nYes, **async_tokio exists** as a feature for criterion 0.8.2.\n\n## Complete Feature List\n\nThe available features are:\n\n1. **async** - Base async support\n2. **async_futures** - Async with futures dependency\n3. **async_smol** - Async with smol runtime\n4. **async_tokio** - Async with tokio runtime\n5. **cargo_bench_support** - Cargo benchmarking integration\n6. **csv_output** - CSV report generation\n7. **default** - Includes rayon, plotters, and cargo_bench_support\n8. **html_reports** - HTML report generation\n9. **plotters** - Plotting support\n10. **rayon** - Parallel processing\n11. **real_blackbox** - Real blackbox optimization\n12. **stable** - Comprehensive feature set combining CSV, HTML, and all async variants\n\nThe async_tokio feature specifically enables tokio-based asynchronous benchmarking capabilities within the library."}]},"uuid":"eda85f84-cf9c-4fd4-8cfc-6c2b83bef752","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:09:01.573Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"4f945cad-db12-4c28-9c7d-a14bf8551117","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:09:01.574Z"}
