{"parentUuid":"71c480c4-31e0-4d9e-b4e0-699a222160aa","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:09:50.094Z","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SMQGeZx2CBqTxYNuwkWCYG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VFsKWAeJ7qBNvYNZCt74V4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh api repos/Shadylukin/Neumann/dependabot/alerts/26 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nvuln = d.get('security_vulnerability',{})\nprint('State:', d.get('state'))\nprint('Package:', vuln.get('package',{}).get('name'))\nprint('Vulnerable range:', vuln.get('vulnerable_version_range'))\nprint('First patched:', vuln.get('first_patched_version',{}).get('identifier','?'))\ndep = d.get('dependency',{})\nprint('Manifest:', dep.get('manifest_path'))\nprint('Scope:', dep.get('scope'))\n\" 2>/dev/null","description":"Get alert #26 full details"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":71342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":289,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYz7E9e1qQRs4uM3ycEwK","uuid":"ed6fce50-8373-4eb5-bda8-aae014d142be"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"4a92d983-b731-4a29-8cf7-2b3cb62a785e","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:09:50.095Z"}
{"parentUuid":"4a92d983-b731-4a29-8cf7-2b3cb62a785e","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFsKWAeJ7qBNvYNZCt74V4","type":"tool_result","content":"State: open\nPackage: minimatch\nVulnerable range: >= 10.0.0, < 10.2.3\nFirst patched: 10.2.3\nManifest: neumann-ts/package-lock.json\nScope: development","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ca751339-8fc6-4045-8f81-6387cb9ace86","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:09:50.610Z"},"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_011vunxUjTLB2UEc3fQjFCEq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","uuid":"1dfc5ae3-4837-4d55-9f8d-807ced8cb16b","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:09:50.611Z"}
{"parentUuid":"1dfc5ae3-4837-4d55-9f8d-807ced8cb16b","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"type":"hook_progress","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","hookName":"PostToolUse:Agent","command":"entire hooks claude-code post-task"},"parentToolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","toolUseID":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:10:49.518Z","uuid":"abda8e04-d34a-4b93-b6b4-1a5c557a23bb"}
{"parentUuid":"a5f2709e-3f6f-4f49-b932-e060fe2ef843","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PzySmwPEeqADbqkJdeKhub","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Alert #26 is about minimatch in the `>= 10.0.0, < 10.2.3` range. But the lockfile shows no minimatch 10.x installed. This is a false positive from Dependabot -- it's tracking a vulnerability range that doesn't actually match any installed package. The actual 3.x and 9.x alerts (#11-#18) are all already **fixed**.\n\nNow I have all the information needed for a comprehensive plan. Here is my complete analysis and implementation plan.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan: Remaining Neumann PRs and Security Fixes\n\n### 1. PR #42: criterion 0.5 -> 0.8\n\n**Analysis:**\n\n- **MSRV concern**: criterion 0.8 requires Rust 1.86. The workspace declares `rust-version = \"1.75\"`. However:\n  - CI only uses `toolchain: stable` (currently 1.92+), never the MSRV\n  - No CI job tests against the declared MSRV\n  - The local machine runs Rust 1.92\n  - The MSRV declaration is therefore aspirational, not enforced\n- **API compatibility**: The only breaking change in criterion 0.6-0.8 is \"Drop async-std support.\" The project does not use async-std with criterion. All APIs used across the 16 crates with bench targets (`criterion_group!`, `criterion_main!`, `black_box`, `BenchmarkId`, `Criterion`, `Throughput`, `BatchSize::SmallInput`, `bench_function`, `bench_with_input`, `iter_batched`) remain unchanged.\n- **Feature compatibility**: The workspace uses `features = [\"html_reports\"]` and two crates use `features = [\"async_tokio\"]`. Both features exist in criterion 0.8.2.\n\n**Decision**: Merge PR #42 with one accompanying change: bump `rust-version` from `\"1.75\"` to `\"1.86\"` in the workspace Cargo.toml. This is the honest thing to do -- criterion 0.8 transitively raises the effective MSRV, and the declared MSRV should reflect reality.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Check out the `dependabot/cargo/criterion-0.8.2` branch\n2. Edit `Cargo.toml` line 37: change `rust-version = \"1.75\"` to `rust-version = \"1.86\"`\n3. Run `cargo build` to verify compilation\n4. Run `cargo nextest run` on a representative crate with benchmarks to verify bench compilation (benches use `#[cfg(test)]` equivalents indirectly via criterion_group, so a full test run is sufficient)\n5. Commit and push the MSRV bump\n6. Merge PR #42\n\n### 2. PR #43: tabled 0.17 -> 0.20\n\n**Analysis:**\n\n- **API compatibility investigation**: The file `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs` is the only consumer of tabled in the entire workspace. It uses exactly:\n  - `Table::from_iter(data)` -- exists in both 0.17 and 0.20 (via `FromIterator` trait impl)\n  - `.with(Style::rounded())` -- exists in both, same import path `tabled::settings::Style`\n  - `.with(Modify::new(Rows::first()).with(Alignment::center()))` -- exists in both, same import path `tabled::settings::{Modify, Alignment}` and `tabled::settings::object::Rows`\n  - `.to_string()` -- exists in both via `Display` impl\n- **Changelog items that could affect us**:\n  - \"Renamed `Columns::single` into `Columns::one`\" and \"Renamed `Rows::single` into `Rows::one`\" -- we use `Rows::first()`, not `Rows::single()`, so this is NOT a concern\n  - \"Changed `with(Border)` logic to set only outer border instead of border of all cells\" -- we do NOT use `Border`, only `Style::rounded()`, so NOT a concern\n- **MSRV**: tabled 0.20.0 has `rust_version = null` (no MSRV constraint)\n\n**Decision**: PR #43 should merge without any code changes to `table.rs`. The Dependabot-generated version bump in `neumann_shell/Cargo.toml` (line 31: `tabled = { version = \"0.17\" ... }` to `\"0.20\"`) is sufficient.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Check out the `dependabot/cargo/tabled-0.20.0` branch\n2. Run `cargo build --package neumann` to verify compilation\n3. Run `cargo nextest run --package neumann` to verify all tests pass (including the 5 table tests in `table.rs`)\n4. Verify the table output still looks correct (the `Style::rounded()` behavior is unchanged)\n5. Merge PR #43\n\n### 3. aws-lc-sys Security Alerts (#19-#24)\n\n**Analysis:**\n\nThe dependency chain for both lockfiles is:\n- **Main Cargo.lock**: `tonic 0.14` -> `rustls 0.23.36` -> `aws-lc-rs 1.16.0` -> `aws-lc-sys 0.37.1`\n- **neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock**: `tensor_chain` -> `tokio-rustls 0.26` -> `rustls 0.23.36` -> `aws-lc-rs 1.15.4` -> `aws-lc-sys 0.37.0`\n\nThe fix requires aws-lc-sys >= 0.38.0. The key constraint:\n- `aws-lc-rs 1.16.0` depends on `aws-lc-sys ^0.37.0` -- CANNOT resolve to 0.38.0\n- `aws-lc-rs 1.16.1` depends on `aws-lc-sys ^0.38.0` -- WILL resolve to 0.38.0\n- `aws-lc-rs 1.15.4` depends on `aws-lc-sys ^0.37.0` -- CANNOT resolve to 0.38.0\n- `rustls 0.23.36` and `0.23.37` both depend on `aws-lc-rs ^1.14` -- allows 1.16.1\n\n**Decision**: `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` will update aws-lc-rs to 1.16.1, which will pull in aws-lc-sys 0.38.0. This is sufficient for the main Cargo.lock. For the Python native lockfile, `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` must be run from within `neumann-py/neumann-native/`.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. From the workspace root: `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs`\n   - This will update: `aws-lc-rs 1.16.0 -> 1.16.1`, `aws-lc-sys 0.37.1 -> 0.38.0`\n2. Verify the main Cargo.lock now has aws-lc-sys 0.38.0\n3. From `neumann-py/neumann-native/`: `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs`\n   - This will update: `aws-lc-rs 1.15.4 -> 1.16.1`, `aws-lc-sys 0.37.0 -> 0.38.0`\n4. Verify the Python native Cargo.lock now has aws-lc-sys 0.38.0\n5. Run `cargo build` from workspace root to verify compilation\n6. Run `cargo nextest run --package tensor_chain` and `cargo nextest run --package neumann_server` (the crates using rustls/tls features) to verify no regressions\n7. Commit both lockfile changes\n8. This should resolve alerts #19, #20, #21, #22, #23, #24\n\n**Note on PR #67**: PR #67 bumps rustls from 0.23.36 to 0.23.37 but does NOT bump aws-lc-rs/aws-lc-sys. If PR #67 is merged first, you still need a separate `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` step. If you want to combine them, you could merge PR #67 first, then do the aws-lc-rs update on main.\n\n### 4. minimatch ReDoS Alert (#26)\n\n**Analysis:**\n\nAlert #26 (CVE-2026-27903) reports minimatch vulnerable in range `>= 10.0.0, < 10.2.3`. But the lockfile shows only minimatch versions 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 installed -- NO minimatch 10.x exists. This is a **false positive** from Dependabot.\n\nThe related alerts for the 3.x and 9.x versions of the same CVEs are all already marked **fixed**:\n- #11 (CVE-2026-26996, 9.x): fixed\n- #12 (CVE-2026-26996, 3.x): fixed  \n- #15 (CVE-2026-27904, 9.x): fixed\n- #16 (CVE-2026-27904, 3.x): fixed\n- #17 (CVE-2026-27903, 9.x): fixed\n- #18 (CVE-2026-27903, 3.x): fixed\n\n**Decision**: Dismiss alert #26 as a false positive. No code or lockfile changes are needed.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Dismiss alert #26 via the GitHub API:\n   ```\n   gh api repos/Shadylukin/Neumann/dependabot/alerts/26 -X PATCH -f state=dismissed -f dismissed_reason=not_impacted -f dismissed_comment=\"No minimatch 10.x is installed. Only 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 are in the lockfile, and both are patched (alerts #17/#18 for 3.x and 9.x are already fixed).\"\n   ```\n\n### Recommended Execution Order\n\n1. **aws-lc-sys fix** (alerts #19-#24) -- standalone lockfile update, no code changes, lowest risk\n2. **Dismiss alert #26** -- no code changes, just a GitHub API call\n3. **Merge PR #43** (tabled 0.20) -- no code changes needed beyond Dependabot's version bump\n4. **Merge PR #42** (criterion 0.8) -- requires MSRV bump in Cargo.toml\n5. **Consider PR #67** (grouped minor bumps) -- independent, can be merged at any time\n\nItems 1-2 can be done as a single commit on main. Items 3-4 are separate PR merges. Item 5 is independent.\n\n### Risk Assessment\n\n| Item | Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| criterion 0.8 | Low -- MSRV bump is the only concern | Bump rust-version to 1.86; CI already uses stable (1.92) |\n| tabled 0.20 | Very low -- API is identical for our usage | Run neumann_shell tests to verify |\n| aws-lc-sys 0.38 | Low -- purely a lockfile update, no API changes | Build + test tensor_chain and neumann_server |\n| minimatch alert #26 | None -- false positive | Dismiss with explanation |\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/Cargo.toml` - MSRV bump (line 37: rust-version), criterion version (line 98)\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs` - Verify unchanged after tabled 0.20 (no changes expected)\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/Cargo.lock` - Main lockfile for aws-lc-sys update\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock` - Python native lockfile for aws-lc-sys update\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann_shell/Cargo.toml` - tabled version bump (line 31)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ad55a98516aea1158 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 75379\ntool_uses: 96\nduration_ms: 776212</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"f61a21ff-ec63-43a6-9bae-4d9d9c0a0f86","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:10:49.516Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to plan fixes for the remaining items in the Neumann project. Here's the context:\n\n## Remaining PRs\n1. **PR #42 (criterion 0.5 → 0.8)**: CI passes (except Docker vulnerability scan, which is infrastructure). No code changes needed — API is backward compatible. The only concern is MSRV (criterion 0.8 needs Rust 1.86, project says rust-version = \"1.75\").\n2. **PR #43 (tabled 0.17 → 0.20)**: CI passes (same Docker scan issue). May need code changes in neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs. Uses `Rows::first()`, `Style::rounded()`, `Table::from_iter()`.\n\n## Security Alerts (6 alerts, 3 CVEs across 2 lock files)\n### aws-lc-sys vulnerabilities (alerts #19-24):\n- Current: aws-lc-sys 0.37.1 in Cargo.lock, 0.37.0 in neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock\n- Fix needed: aws-lc-sys >= 0.38.0 (patches PKCS7_verify bypass and AES-CCM timing side-channel)\n- Dependency chain: tonic → rustls → aws-lc-rs → aws-lc-sys\n- Need to check if `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` suffices or if upstream deps need bumping\n\n### minimatch ReDoS (alert #26):\n- Vulnerable minimatch 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 in neumann-ts/package-lock.json\n- Fix: need minimatch >= 10.0.1\n- eslint and @typescript-eslint packages depend on it\n- PR #57 (eslint v10) was already merged, PR #55 (@typescript-eslint/parser 8.56.1) was merged — these may have partially fixed it\n\n## Key Questions to Address in Plan:\n1. Can we merge PR #42 given the MSRV concern (criterion 0.8 requires Rust 1.86 but we declare 1.75)?\n2. For PR #43, what exact code changes are needed in table.rs?\n3. For aws-lc-sys: can `cargo update -p aws-lc-sys` get us to 0.38+, or do we need to bump tonic/rustls?\n4. For minimatch: after merging PRs #55 and #57, is the vulnerability resolved or do we need more npm updates?\n\nPlease design a concrete implementation plan for addressing all of these.","agentId":"ad55a98516aea1158","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Alert #26 is about minimatch in the `>= 10.0.0, < 10.2.3` range. But the lockfile shows no minimatch 10.x installed. This is a false positive from Dependabot -- it's tracking a vulnerability range that doesn't actually match any installed package. The actual 3.x and 9.x alerts (#11-#18) are all already **fixed**.\n\nNow I have all the information needed for a comprehensive plan. Here is my complete analysis and implementation plan.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan: Remaining Neumann PRs and Security Fixes\n\n### 1. PR #42: criterion 0.5 -> 0.8\n\n**Analysis:**\n\n- **MSRV concern**: criterion 0.8 requires Rust 1.86. The workspace declares `rust-version = \"1.75\"`. However:\n  - CI only uses `toolchain: stable` (currently 1.92+), never the MSRV\n  - No CI job tests against the declared MSRV\n  - The local machine runs Rust 1.92\n  - The MSRV declaration is therefore aspirational, not enforced\n- **API compatibility**: The only breaking change in criterion 0.6-0.8 is \"Drop async-std support.\" The project does not use async-std with criterion. All APIs used across the 16 crates with bench targets (`criterion_group!`, `criterion_main!`, `black_box`, `BenchmarkId`, `Criterion`, `Throughput`, `BatchSize::SmallInput`, `bench_function`, `bench_with_input`, `iter_batched`) remain unchanged.\n- **Feature compatibility**: The workspace uses `features = [\"html_reports\"]` and two crates use `features = [\"async_tokio\"]`. Both features exist in criterion 0.8.2.\n\n**Decision**: Merge PR #42 with one accompanying change: bump `rust-version` from `\"1.75\"` to `\"1.86\"` in the workspace Cargo.toml. This is the honest thing to do -- criterion 0.8 transitively raises the effective MSRV, and the declared MSRV should reflect reality.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Check out the `dependabot/cargo/criterion-0.8.2` branch\n2. Edit `Cargo.toml` line 37: change `rust-version = \"1.75\"` to `rust-version = \"1.86\"`\n3. Run `cargo build` to verify compilation\n4. Run `cargo nextest run` on a representative crate with benchmarks to verify bench compilation (benches use `#[cfg(test)]` equivalents indirectly via criterion_group, so a full test run is sufficient)\n5. Commit and push the MSRV bump\n6. Merge PR #42\n\n### 2. PR #43: tabled 0.17 -> 0.20\n\n**Analysis:**\n\n- **API compatibility investigation**: The file `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs` is the only consumer of tabled in the entire workspace. It uses exactly:\n  - `Table::from_iter(data)` -- exists in both 0.17 and 0.20 (via `FromIterator` trait impl)\n  - `.with(Style::rounded())` -- exists in both, same import path `tabled::settings::Style`\n  - `.with(Modify::new(Rows::first()).with(Alignment::center()))` -- exists in both, same import path `tabled::settings::{Modify, Alignment}` and `tabled::settings::object::Rows`\n  - `.to_string()` -- exists in both via `Display` impl\n- **Changelog items that could affect us**:\n  - \"Renamed `Columns::single` into `Columns::one`\" and \"Renamed `Rows::single` into `Rows::one`\" -- we use `Rows::first()`, not `Rows::single()`, so this is NOT a concern\n  - \"Changed `with(Border)` logic to set only outer border instead of border of all cells\" -- we do NOT use `Border`, only `Style::rounded()`, so NOT a concern\n- **MSRV**: tabled 0.20.0 has `rust_version = null` (no MSRV constraint)\n\n**Decision**: PR #43 should merge without any code changes to `table.rs`. The Dependabot-generated version bump in `neumann_shell/Cargo.toml` (line 31: `tabled = { version = \"0.17\" ... }` to `\"0.20\"`) is sufficient.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Check out the `dependabot/cargo/tabled-0.20.0` branch\n2. Run `cargo build --package neumann` to verify compilation\n3. Run `cargo nextest run --package neumann` to verify all tests pass (including the 5 table tests in `table.rs`)\n4. Verify the table output still looks correct (the `Style::rounded()` behavior is unchanged)\n5. Merge PR #43\n\n### 3. aws-lc-sys Security Alerts (#19-#24)\n\n**Analysis:**\n\nThe dependency chain for both lockfiles is:\n- **Main Cargo.lock**: `tonic 0.14` -> `rustls 0.23.36` -> `aws-lc-rs 1.16.0` -> `aws-lc-sys 0.37.1`\n- **neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock**: `tensor_chain` -> `tokio-rustls 0.26` -> `rustls 0.23.36` -> `aws-lc-rs 1.15.4` -> `aws-lc-sys 0.37.0`\n\nThe fix requires aws-lc-sys >= 0.38.0. The key constraint:\n- `aws-lc-rs 1.16.0` depends on `aws-lc-sys ^0.37.0` -- CANNOT resolve to 0.38.0\n- `aws-lc-rs 1.16.1` depends on `aws-lc-sys ^0.38.0` -- WILL resolve to 0.38.0\n- `aws-lc-rs 1.15.4` depends on `aws-lc-sys ^0.37.0` -- CANNOT resolve to 0.38.0\n- `rustls 0.23.36` and `0.23.37` both depend on `aws-lc-rs ^1.14` -- allows 1.16.1\n\n**Decision**: `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` will update aws-lc-rs to 1.16.1, which will pull in aws-lc-sys 0.38.0. This is sufficient for the main Cargo.lock. For the Python native lockfile, `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` must be run from within `neumann-py/neumann-native/`.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. From the workspace root: `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs`\n   - This will update: `aws-lc-rs 1.16.0 -> 1.16.1`, `aws-lc-sys 0.37.1 -> 0.38.0`\n2. Verify the main Cargo.lock now has aws-lc-sys 0.38.0\n3. From `neumann-py/neumann-native/`: `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs`\n   - This will update: `aws-lc-rs 1.15.4 -> 1.16.1`, `aws-lc-sys 0.37.0 -> 0.38.0`\n4. Verify the Python native Cargo.lock now has aws-lc-sys 0.38.0\n5. Run `cargo build` from workspace root to verify compilation\n6. Run `cargo nextest run --package tensor_chain` and `cargo nextest run --package neumann_server` (the crates using rustls/tls features) to verify no regressions\n7. Commit both lockfile changes\n8. This should resolve alerts #19, #20, #21, #22, #23, #24\n\n**Note on PR #67**: PR #67 bumps rustls from 0.23.36 to 0.23.37 but does NOT bump aws-lc-rs/aws-lc-sys. If PR #67 is merged first, you still need a separate `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` step. If you want to combine them, you could merge PR #67 first, then do the aws-lc-rs update on main.\n\n### 4. minimatch ReDoS Alert (#26)\n\n**Analysis:**\n\nAlert #26 (CVE-2026-27903) reports minimatch vulnerable in range `>= 10.0.0, < 10.2.3`. But the lockfile shows only minimatch versions 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 installed -- NO minimatch 10.x exists. This is a **false positive** from Dependabot.\n\nThe related alerts for the 3.x and 9.x versions of the same CVEs are all already marked **fixed**:\n- #11 (CVE-2026-26996, 9.x): fixed\n- #12 (CVE-2026-26996, 3.x): fixed  \n- #15 (CVE-2026-27904, 9.x): fixed\n- #16 (CVE-2026-27904, 3.x): fixed\n- #17 (CVE-2026-27903, 9.x): fixed\n- #18 (CVE-2026-27903, 3.x): fixed\n\n**Decision**: Dismiss alert #26 as a false positive. No code or lockfile changes are needed.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Dismiss alert #26 via the GitHub API:\n   ```\n   gh api repos/Shadylukin/Neumann/dependabot/alerts/26 -X PATCH -f state=dismissed -f dismissed_reason=not_impacted -f dismissed_comment=\"No minimatch 10.x is installed. Only 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 are in the lockfile, and both are patched (alerts #17/#18 for 3.x and 9.x are already fixed).\"\n   ```\n\n### Recommended Execution Order\n\n1. **aws-lc-sys fix** (alerts #19-#24) -- standalone lockfile update, no code changes, lowest risk\n2. **Dismiss alert #26** -- no code changes, just a GitHub API call\n3. **Merge PR #43** (tabled 0.20) -- no code changes needed beyond Dependabot's version bump\n4. **Merge PR #42** (criterion 0.8) -- requires MSRV bump in Cargo.toml\n5. **Consider PR #67** (grouped minor bumps) -- independent, can be merged at any time\n\nItems 1-2 can be done as a single commit on main. Items 3-4 are separate PR merges. Item 5 is independent.\n\n### Risk Assessment\n\n| Item | Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| criterion 0.8 | Low -- MSRV bump is the only concern | Bump rust-version to 1.86; CI already uses stable (1.92) |\n| tabled 0.20 | Very low -- API is identical for our usage | Run neumann_shell tests to verify |\n| aws-lc-sys 0.38 | Low -- purely a lockfile update, no API changes | Build + test tensor_chain and neumann_server |\n| minimatch alert #26 | None -- false positive | Dismiss with explanation |\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/Cargo.toml` - MSRV bump (line 37: rust-version), criterion version (line 98)\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs` - Verify unchanged after tabled 0.20 (no changes expected)\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/Cargo.lock` - Main lockfile for aws-lc-sys update\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock` - Python native lockfile for aws-lc-sys update\n- `/Users/lukin/Neumann/neumann_shell/Cargo.toml` - tabled version bump (line 31)"}],"totalDurationMs":776212,"tota