{"parentUuid":"b7324ab7-1fb7-49c6-85d4-e618c1574868","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012XkKUBqjoNGT1DEoNjT1HR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LnuVPwni2kPKyv6yDXajJb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/lukin/.claude/plans/mighty-hugging-umbrella.md","content":"# Plan: Clear Remaining PRs + Fix Security Alerts\n\n## Context\n\nAfter merging PR #65 and 8 Dependabot PRs, 2 PRs remain open (#42, #43) and 6 Dependabot security alerts need resolution (aws-lc-sys CVEs + minimatch ReDoS). All items are low-risk dependency updates — no application logic changes.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Fix aws-lc-sys Security Alerts (#19-24)\n\n**Problem**: aws-lc-sys 0.37.x has 3 CVEs (PKCS7_verify bypass x2, AES-CCM timing side-channel). Affects both `Cargo.lock` (0.37.1) and `neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock` (0.37.0).\n\n**Fix**: `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` bumps aws-lc-rs 1.16.0 → 1.16.1 which pulls aws-lc-sys 0.38.0 (patched). No code changes — lockfile-only.\n\n**Commands**:\n```bash\n# Main workspace\ncargo update -p aws-lc-rs\ngrep 'aws-lc-sys' Cargo.lock  # verify 0.38.0\n\n# Python native\ncd neumann-py/neumann-native && cargo update -p aws-lc-rs\ngrep 'aws-lc-sys' Cargo.lock  # verify 0.38.0\n\n# Verify build\ncargo build --package neumann_server\ncargo nextest run --package neumann_server\n```\n\n**Files**: `Cargo.lock`, `neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock`\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Dismiss minimatch Alert #26\n\n**Problem**: Alert #26 flags minimatch ReDoS for range `>= 10.0.0, < 10.2.3`. But no minimatch 10.x is installed — only 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 exist in the lockfile. This is a false positive.\n\n**Fix**: Dismiss via API.\n\n```bash\ngh api repos/Shadylukin/Neumann/dependabot/alerts/26 \\\n  -X PATCH -f state=dismissed -f dismissed_reason=not_impacted \\\n  -f dismissed_comment=\"No minimatch 10.x installed. Only 3.x and 9.x in lockfile.\"\n```\n\n**Files**: None\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Merge PR #43 (tabled 0.17 → 0.20)\n\n**Problem**: tabled major version bump in neumann_shell.\n\n**Analysis**: CI passes (Clippy, Test, all platforms). The only tabled consumer is `neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs` which uses `Table::from_iter()`, `Style::rounded()`, `Rows::first()`, `Modify`, `Alignment` — all unchanged in 0.20. No code changes needed.\n\n**Fix**: Merge directly.\n\n```bash\ngh pr merge 43 --repo Shadylukin/Neumann --squash --delete-branch\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Merge PR #42 (criterion 0.5 → 0.8)\n\n**Problem**: criterion major version bump. MSRV concern: criterion 0.8 requires Rust 1.86, workspace declares `rust-version = \"1.75\"`.\n\n**Analysis**: CI passes (all 16 bench targets compile and run). The criterion API used across all bench files (`criterion_group!`, `criterion_main!`, `bench_function`, `BenchmarkId`, `Throughput`, `black_box`) is unchanged. No MSRV CI job exists — only `toolchain: stable` (1.92+) is tested. The `rust-version = \"1.75\"` is aspirational and not enforced.\n\n**Fix**: Bump MSRV to match reality, then merge.\n\n```bash\n# On the PR branch, bump MSRV\ngh pr checkout 42\n# Edit Cargo.toml line 37: rust-version = \"1.75\" → \"1.86\"\ncargo build --package graph_engine  # verify\ngit add Cargo.toml && git commit -m \"Bump rust-version to 1.86 for criterion 0.8 compatibility\"\ngit push\ngh pr merge 42 --squash --delete-branch\n```\n\n**Files**: `Cargo.toml` (line 37)\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Commit aws-lc-sys fix + push\n\nCreate a single commit on main with both lockfile updates from Step 1.\n\n```bash\ngit add Cargo.lock neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock\ngit commit -m \"Update aws-lc-rs to 1.16.1 to fix aws-lc-sys CVEs\"\ngit push\n```\n\n---\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter all steps:\n```bash\n# Security audit\ncargo audit\n\n# Confirm no open alerts\ngh api repos/Shadylukin/Neumann/dependabot/alerts --jq '[.[] | select(.state==\"open\")] | length'\n\n# Confirm no open PRs\ngh pr list --repo Shadylukin/Neumann --state open\n```\n\n## Execution Order\n\n1. aws-lc-sys lockfile update (Step 1 + 5) — on main, standalone commit\n2. Dismiss alert #26 (Step 2) — API call only\n3. Merge PR #43 tabled (Step 3) — direct merge\n4. Merge PR #42 criterion (Step 4) — requires MSRV edit on PR branch first\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":325,"cache_read_input_tokens":152142,"output_tokens":1473,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":325,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CYz7Lm6tBHgFmc639vuVx","type":"assistant","uuid":"6986df17-cb58-4ced-83ae-77dfad3afaa2","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:11:44.170Z"}
{"parentUuid":"6986df17-cb58-4ced-83ae-77dfad3afaa2","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"progress","data":{"type":"hook_progress","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","hookName":"PostToolUse:Write","command":"callback"},"parentToolUseID":"toolu_01LnuVPwni2kPKyv6yDXajJb","toolUseID":"toolu_01LnuVPwni2kPKyv6yDXajJb","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:11:44.268Z","uuid":"a1f81c89-8d7c-4fa9-a339-03600076651e"}
{"parentUuid":"6986df17-cb58-4ced-83ae-77dfad3afaa2","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LnuVPwni2kPKyv6yDXajJb","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/lukin/.claude/plans/mighty-hugging-umbrella.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"5a1e6142-d4fc-4579-9832-87e69e4242c5","timestamp":"2026-03-13T00:11:44.268Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/lukin/.claude/plans/mighty-hugging-umbrella.md","content":"# Plan: Clear Remaining PRs + Fix Security Alerts\n\n## Context\n\nAfter merging PR #65 and 8 Dependabot PRs, 2 PRs remain open (#42, #43) and 6 Dependabot security alerts need resolution (aws-lc-sys CVEs + minimatch ReDoS). All items are low-risk dependency updates — no application logic changes.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Fix aws-lc-sys Security Alerts (#19-24)\n\n**Problem**: aws-lc-sys 0.37.x has 3 CVEs (PKCS7_verify bypass x2, AES-CCM timing side-channel). Affects both `Cargo.lock` (0.37.1) and `neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock` (0.37.0).\n\n**Fix**: `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` bumps aws-lc-rs 1.16.0 → 1.16.1 which pulls aws-lc-sys 0.38.0 (patched). No code changes — lockfile-only.\n\n**Commands**:\n```bash\n# Main workspace\ncargo update -p aws-lc-rs\ngrep 'aws-lc-sys' Cargo.lock  # verify 0.38.0\n\n# Python native\ncd neumann-py/neumann-native && cargo update -p aws-lc-rs\ngrep 'aws-lc-sys' Cargo.lock  # verify 0.38.0\n\n# Verify build\ncargo build --package neumann_server\ncargo nextest run --package neumann_server\n```\n\n**Files**: `Cargo.lock`, `neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock`\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Dismiss minimatch Alert #26\n\n**Problem**: Alert #26 flags minimatch ReDoS for range `>= 10.0.0, < 10.2.3`. But no minimatch 10.x is installed — only 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 exist in the lockfile. This is a false positive.\n\n**Fix**: Dismiss via API.\n\n```bash\ngh api repos/Shadylukin/Neumann/dependabot/alerts/26 \\\n  -X PATCH -f state=dismissed -f dismissed_reason=not_impacted \\\n  -f dismissed_comment=\"No minimatch 10.x installed. Only 3.x and 9.x in lockfile.\"\n```\n\n**Files**: None\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Merge PR #43 (tabled 0.17 → 0.20)\n\n**Problem**: tabled major version bump in neumann_shell.\n\n**Analysis**: CI passes (Clippy, Test, all platforms). The only tabled consumer is `neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs` which uses `Table::from_iter()`, `Style::rounded()`, `Rows::first()`, `Modify`, `Alignment` — all unchanged in 0.20. No code changes needed.\n\n**Fix**: Merge directly.\n\n```bash\ngh pr merge 43 --repo Shadylukin/Neumann --squash --delete-branch\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Merge PR #42 (criterion 0.5 → 0.8)\n\n**Problem**: criterion major version bump. MSRV concern: criterion 0.8 requires Rust 1.86, workspace declares `rust-version = \"1.75\"`.\n\n**Analysis**: CI passes (all 16 bench targets compile and run). The criterion API used across all bench files (`criterion_group!`, `criterion_main!`, `bench_function`, `BenchmarkId`, `Throughput`, `black_box`) is unchanged. No MSRV CI job exists — only `toolchain: stable` (1.92+) is tested. The `rust-version = \"1.75\"` is aspirational and not enforced.\n\n**Fix**: Bump MSRV to match reality, then merge.\n\n```bash\n# On the PR branch, bump MSRV\ngh pr checkout 42\n# Edit Cargo.toml line 37: rust-version = \"1.75\" → \"1.86\"\ncargo build --package graph_engine  # verify\ngit add Cargo.toml && git commit -m \"Bump rust-version to 1.86 for criterion 0.8 compatibility\"\ngit push\ngh pr merge 42 --squash --delete-branch\n```\n\n**Files**: `Cargo.toml` (line 37)\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Commit aws-lc-sys fix + push\n\nCreate a single commit on main with both lockfile updates from Step 1.\n\n```bash\ngit add Cargo.lock neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock\ngit commit -m \"Update aws-lc-rs to 1.16.1 to fix aws-lc-sys CVEs\"\ngit push\n```\n\n---\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter all steps:\n```bash\n# Security audit\ncargo audit\n\n# Confirm no open alerts\ngh api repos/Shadylukin/Neumann/dependabot/alerts --jq '[.[] | select(.state==\"open\")] | length'\n\n# Confirm no open PRs\ngh pr list --repo Shadylukin/Neumann --state open\n```\n\n## Execution Order\n\n1. aws-lc-sys lockfile update (Step 1 + 5) — on main, standalone commit\n2. Dismiss alert #26 (Step 2) — API call only\n3. Merge PR #43 tabled (Step 3) — direct merge\n4. Merge PR #42 criterion (Step 4) — requires MSRV edit on PR branch first\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":611,"newStart":1,"newLines":117,"lines":["-# Plan: Fix State Persistence Correctness + Improve Compression","+# Plan: Clear Remaining PRs + Fix Security Alerts"," "," ## Context"," ","-Audit of Neumann's snapshot/checkpoint system found correctness bugs in the restore path, a circular dependency where checkpoint blobs pollute the store they snapshot, and unused compression infrastructure. This plan fixes the foundation first, then layers on compression.","+After merging PR #65 and 8 Dependabot PRs, 2 PRs remain open (#42, #43) and 6 Dependabot security alerts need resolution (aws-lc-sys CVEs + minimatch ReDoS). All items are low-risk dependency updates — no application logic changes."," ","-**Already working well:**","-- Embeddings use `CompressedEmbedding` (TT >=256-dim, sparse >50% zeros) — `embedding_slab.rs:538`","-- File-based snapshots (`save_v3`/`load_v3`) use bitcode + zstd + typed `SlabRouter::restore()` — `snapshot.rs:285,369`","-- Atomic writes via temp file + rename — `snapshot.rs:326`","-","-**Bugs found:**","-1. `restore_from_bytes()` is lossy — scan+put loses graph/relational/embedding slab state and configs — `lib.rs:1326`","-2. `GraphTensor::restore()` allocates fresh edge IDs, breaking metadata references — `graph_tensor.rs:677,299`","-3. Checkpoint blobs in same TensorStore cause unbounded snapshot growth — `streaming.rs:156`, `slab_router.rs:709`","-4. Checkpoint in-memory path skips zstd — `slab_router.rs:438`","-","-**Restore contract**: `CheckpointManager` guarantees exact `TensorStore` restore. Query-engine cache/schema refresh after rollback is a separate concern and is explicitly **out of scope** for this change.","-"," ---"," ","-## Phase 0a: GraphTensor Edge ID Preservation","+## Step 1: Fix aws-lc-sys Security Alerts (#19-24)"," ","-**Bug**: `restore()` calls `add_edge()` → `next_edge_id.fetch_add(1)` (line 299). Edges [0,1,3,5] become [0,1,2,3], breaking `edge:*` metadata keys from `edge_data`.","+**Problem**: aws-lc-sys 0.37.x has 3 CVEs (PKCS7_verify bypass x2, AES-CCM timing side-channel). Affects both `Cargo.lock` (0.37.1) and `neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock` (0.37.0)."," ","-**File**: `tensor_store/src/graph_tensor.rs`","-- Add `fn add_edge_with_id(&self, edge_id: EdgeId, from, to, edge_type, directed)` — same as `add_edge()` but uses provided ID, no fetch_add","-- Change `restore()` (line 660-696):","-  - Move `next_edge_id.store(snapshot.next_edge_id, ...)` BEFORE edge loop","-  - Replace `add_edge(...)` with `add_edge_with_id(edge.edge_id, ...)`","+**Fix**: `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` bumps aws-lc-rs 1.16.0 → 1.16.1 which pulls aws-lc-sys 0.38.0 (patched). No code changes — lockfile-only."," ","-**Tests:**","-- Roundtrip with non-sequential IDs [0,1,3,5,100] → verify exact IDs preserved","-- Edge metadata under `edge:3` maps to correct edge after restore","-- Graph with deletions → snapshot → restore → full fidelity check","+**Commands**:","+```bash","+# Main workspace","+cargo update -p aws-lc-rs","+grep 'aws-lc-sys' Cargo.lock  # verify 0.38.0"," ","----","+# Python native","+cd neumann-py/neumann-native && cargo update -p aws-lc-rs","+grep 'aws-lc-sys' Cargo.lock  # verify 0.38.0"," ","-## Phase 0b: Arc\\<ArcSwap\\> Router for Faithful Restore","-","-**Bug**: `restore_from_bytes()` creates a new `SlabRouter` via `from_bytes()` (correct) but can't swap it into `Arc<SlabRouter>`. Falls back to `scan(\"\") + put()` which routes `node:*/edge:*/table:*` to metadata only (slab_router.rs:189-198), losing graph CSR, relational columns, embeddings, and slab configs (`dimension`, `capacity`, `strategy`, `segment_size`).","-","-**Why Arc\\<ArcSwap\\>**: `TensorStore` is `Clone` with shared-storage semantics (lib.rs:776). `BlobStore::new(store.clone())` (lib.rs:87, query_router:1034) relies on all clones seeing the same data. `Arc<ArcSwap<SlabRouter>>` ensures all clones share one swap cell — after restore, every clone (including BlobStore's) sees the new router.","-","-**Files:**","-- `tensor_store/Cargo.toml` — Add `arc-swap = \"1\"`","-- `tensor_store/src/lib.rs` (17 `self.router.` call sites):","-  - `router: Arc<SlabRouter>` → `router: Arc<ArcSwap<SlabRouter>>` (line 779)","-  - Constructor: `router: Arc::new(ArcSwap::from_pointee(SlabRouter::new()))`","-  - `Clone`: `Arc<ArcSwap<_>>` is Clone via `Arc::clone` — all clones share the swap cell","-  - **`router(&self) -> &SlabRouter`** (line 1026): Cannot return `&SlabRouter` from a transient ArcSwap guard (guard lifetime is too short). Two consumers exist:","-    - `relational_engine/src/lib.rs:2452` — `self.store.router().relations` borrows `&RelationalSlab` through router","-    - `tensor_store/src/lib.rs:3847` — unit test","-","-    **API redesign**: Replace `router()` with `with_router<F, R>(&self, f: F) -> R where F: FnOnce(&SlabRouter) -> R`. This loads the guard once and passes the reference to the closure, keeping the guard alive for the duration. For `RelationalEngine::slab()`:","-    ```rust","-    // Old: &self.store.router().relations","-    // New: Cannot return &RelationalSlab from closure.","-    ```","-    Since `slab()` returns `&RelationalSlab`, and `RelationalSlab` lives inside the guard, this pattern doesn't work for returning references. **Alternative**: `RelationalEngine` caches an `Arc<SlabRouter>` via `load_full()` and refreshes it on a generation counter or subscription. Or: `RelationalEngine::slab()` callers are changed to accept closures. Or: add a dedicated `TensorStore::with_relational_slab<F, R>(&self, f: F) -> R` accessor.","-","-    **Simplest correct approach**: Add `TensorStore::relational_slab(&self) -> Arc<SlabRouter>` that returns `self.router.load_full()` — caller gets an `Arc<SlabRouter>` they can borrow from for the duration of their operation. `RelationalEngine::slab()` becomes:","-    ```rust","-    fn slab_router(&self) -> Arc<SlabRouter> {","-        self.store.load_router()","-    }","-    // Callers: let router = self.slab_router(); let slab = &router.relations; ...","-    ```","-    This requires updating all `slab()` call sites in `relational_engine` to hold the Arc for the scope of their operation.","-","-  - **Multi-access methods**: Any method performing multiple router accesses must `let router = self.router.load();` once at the top and use `router` throughout. Prevents concurrent restore from mixing old and new state.","-  - `store()` method: returns `self.clone()` — engines hold TensorStore clone sharing the swap cell","-  - **`restore_from_bytes()`**:","-    ```","-    let new_router = SlabRouter::from_bytes(bytes)?;","-    self.router.store(Arc::new(new_router));","-    // Rebuild Bloom filter from new router state","-    if let Some(ref filter) = self.bloom_filter {","-        filter.clear();","-        for key in self.router.load().scan(\"\") {","-            filter.add(&key);","-        }","-    }","-    ```","-    Atomic swap + Bloom rebuild. Without rebuild, Bloom-enabled stores return false negatives for keys that existed before the checkpoint but were not re-inserted after. Remove old scan+put path entirely.","-","-**Callers of `TensorStore::router()`** (2 sites — server/shell `router()` returns QueryRouter, not SlabRouter):","-- `relational_engine/src/lib.rs:2452` — see RelationalEngine migration below","-- `tensor_store/src/lib.rs:3847` — unit test → `let r = store.load_router(); assert_eq!(r.len(), 0);`","-","-### RelationalEngine `slab()` Migration (23 call sites)","-","-**Current**: `fn slab(&self) -> &RelationalSlab` (line 2451) returns `&self.store.router().relations`. With `Arc<ArcSwap<SlabRouter>>`, `router()` can't return `&SlabRouter` (guard lifetime too short).","-","-**Migration strategy**: Change `slab()` to return `Arc<SlabRouter>` via `load_full()`. All 23 call sites insert `.relations` into the chain. Since **every call site uses a temporary borrow** (no stored references, no cross-expression lifetimes), this is a mechanical transformation:","-","-```rust","-// Before:","-fn slab(&self) -> &RelationalSlab { &self.store.router().relations }","-self.slab().table_exists(name)","-","-// After:","-fn slab(&self) -> Arc<SlabRouter> { self.store.load_router() }","-self.slab().relations.table_exists(name)","+# Verify build","+cargo build --package neumann_server","+cargo nextest run --package neumann_server"," ```"," ","-**Complete call site list** — each `self.slab().foo()` becomes `self.slab().relations.foo()`:","+**Files**: `Cargo.lock`, `neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock`"," ","-| Line | Method | Expression Pattern |","-|------|--------|--------------------|","-| 2296 | `recover_from_metadata()` | `.table_exists(name)` |","-| 2297 | `recover_from_metadata()` | `.create_table(name, schema)` |","-| 2669 | `create_table()` | `.create_table(name, schema).map_err(...)` |","-| 4748 | `drop_table()` | `.drop_table(table)` |","-| 5299 | `row_count()` | `.row_count(table).map_err(...)` |","-| 5351 | `for_each_row()` | `.scan_for_each(table, &mut \\|...\\|)` |","-| 5999 | `has_columnar_data()` | `.get_schema(table).is_some_and(...)` |","-| 6320 | `select_by_indices()` | `.get_rows_by_indices(table, &indices).ok()?` |","-| 6323 | `select_by_indices()` | `.get_schema(table)?` |","-| 6372 | `apply_condition()` | `.row_count(table).ok()?` |","-| 6378 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |","-| 6392 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |","-| 6405 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |","-| 6418 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |","-| 6431 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |","-| 6444 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |","-| 6457 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_float_column(table, col).ok()?` |","-| 6470 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_float_column(table, col).ok()?` |","-| 6483 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_float_column(table, col).ok()?` |","-| 6672 | `rollback()` | `.delete(table, *slab_row_id)` |","-| 6700 | `rollback()` | `.restore_row(table, *slab_row_id, old_values)` |","-| 7023 | `update()` | `.update_row(table, *id, &updates).map_err(...)?` |","-| 7123 | `delete()` | `.delete(table, *id).map_err(...)?` |","-","-**Methods with multiple `self.slab()` calls in the same scope** must hoist the Arc to avoid loading the router twice (consistency + performance):","-- `recover_from_metadata()` (lines 2296-2297): `let slab = self.slab(); slab.relations.table_exists(...); slab.relations.create_table(...);`","-- `select_by_indices()` (lines 6320,6323): `let slab = self.slab(); slab.relations.get_rows_by_indices(...); slab.relations.get_schema(...);`","-- `apply_condition()` (lines 6372-6483): `let slab = self.slab();` once at top, 10 uses of `slab.relations.*`","-","-**No other crate calls `TensorStore::router()` for `SlabRouter` access** — `neumann_server` and `neumann_shell` have their own `router()` methods returning `QueryRouter`.","-","-**Tests:**","-- Full roundtrip: graph edges+metadata, relational tables+data, embeddings → `snapshot_bytes()` → `restore_from_bytes()` → verify ALL slab state","-- Clone contract: `store.clone()` sees restore from original","-- Config preservation: `EmbeddingSlab.dimension`, `CacheRing.capacity/strategy` survive roundtrip","-- Concurrent reads during restore (ArcSwap guarantees no torn state)","-- Bloom filter rebuild: enable Bloom → put keys → snapshot → restore with different keys → verify old keys found (Bloom rebuilt from new router state, no false negatives)","-"," ---"," ","-## Phase 0c: Decouple Checkpoint Storage — Sync Trait + File Backend","+## Step 2: Dismiss minimatch Alert #26"," ","-**Bug**: `BlobStore` writes `_blob:*` keys into the same TensorStore being snapshotted. Content-addressed chunks are shared via dedup, making selective exclusion unsafe. Each checkpoint captures prior blobs — unbounded growth.","+**Problem**: Alert #26 flags minimatch ReDoS for range `>= 10.0.0, < 10.2.3`. But no minimatch 10.x is installed — only 3.1.5 and 9.0.9 exist in the lockfile. This is a false positive."," ","-**Design decisions:**","-- `CheckpointConfig` stays policy-only: retention, auto-checkpoint, confirmation, preview size","-- Filesystem location is backend-specific: `FileCheckpointStore::new(path)` takes `PathBuf` directly","-- `CheckpointInfo` drops `artifact_id` — replace with `storage_id: String` (opaque handle, kept private to backend) or remove entirely if callers only need `id, name, created_at, size, trigger`","-- Trait is sync: file I/O doesn't benefit from async, eliminates tokio runtime dependency for checkpoint paths","+**Fix**: Dismiss via API."," ","-### New: `tensor_checkpoint/src/checkpoint_store.rs`","-","-```rust","-pub trait CheckpointStore: Send + Sync {","-    fn store(&self, state: &CheckpointState) -> Result<String>;","-    fn load(&self, id_or_name: &str) -> Result<CheckpointState>;","-    fn list(&self) -> Result<Vec<CheckpointInfo>>;","-    fn delete(&self, id_or_name: &str) -> Result<()>;","-}","+```bash","+gh api repos/Shadylukin/Neumann/dependabot/alerts/26 \\","+  -X PATCH -f state=dismissed -f dismissed_reason=not_impacted \\","+  -f dismissed_comment=\"No minimatch 10.x installed. Only 3.x and 9.x in lockfile.\""," ```"," ","-### New: `tensor_checkpoint/src/file_store.rs`","+**Files**: None"," ","-**File format** — two-part for efficient listing:","-```","-[header_len: u32 LE]","-[header: bitcode(CheckpointFileHeader)]","-[body: bitcode(CheckpointBody)]","-```","+---"," ","-`CheckpointFileHeader` (read by `list()`, never reads body):","-```rust","-struct CheckpointFileHeader {","-    id: String,","-    name: String,","-    created_at: u64,","-    trigger: Option<CheckpointTrigger>,  // full trigger, not just String","-    metadata: CheckpointMetadata,         // relational/graph/vector stats","-    body_size: u64,","-}","-```","+## Step 3: Merge PR #43 (tabled 0.17 → 0.20)"," ","-`CheckpointBody` (read only by `load()`):","-```rust","-struct CheckpointBody {","-    store_snapshot: Vec<u8>,","-}","-```","+**Problem**: tabled major version bump in neumann_shell."," ","-On `load()`, both header and body are read → reconstructed into `CheckpointState { id, name, created_at, trigger, store_snapshot, metadata }`. The full `CheckpointState` model is unchanged; the split is internal to the file format.","+**Analysis**: CI passes (Clippy, Test, all platforms). The only tabled consumer is `neumann_shell/src/output/table.rs` which uses `Table::from_iter()`, `Style::rounded()`, `Rows::first()`, `Modify`, `Alignment` — all unchanged in 0.20. No code changes needed."," ","-**Directory source**: `FileCheckpointStore::new(dir: impl Into<PathBuf>)` takes an explicit path. The directory comes from `QueryRouter.checkpoint_dir` which must be set before any checkpoint operation (see \"Checkpoint directory — mandatory, no fallback\" below). No fallback to temp dirs or WAL siblings.","+**Fix**: Merge directly."," ","-**Duplicate name resolution**: When `load(\"name\")` or `delete(\"name\")` matches multiple files by name, resolve to the **newest** by `(created_at DESC, id ASC)`. With `u64` millisecond timestamps, same-millisecond collisions are rare; the secondary `id` sort guarantees deterministic results regardless.","-","-Operations:","-- `store()`: serialize header + body separately, write `[header_len][header][body]` to `{dir}/{id}.ncp` via atomic temp+rename. Create directory if it doesn't exist.","-- `load(id_or_name)`: scan directory headers for matching ID first (exact), then name (newest-first if duplicates). Read full file for match.","-- `list()`: scan `*.ncp` files, read first `4 + header_len` bytes from each → build `CheckpointInfo`. Sort by `created_at` descending (newest first).","-- `delete(id_or_name)`: find matching file (same resolution as `load()`), remove it.","-","-### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/src/state.rs`","-","-- **Timestamp precision**: Keep `created_at` as `u64` but change unit from seconds to **milliseconds**. Update `CheckpointState::new()` (line 31) to use `d.as_millis() as u64` instead of `d.as_secs()`. `u64` millis gives ~584 million years of range — no overflow concern. This eliminates the same-second collision documented in retention tests (retention.rs:124) while keeping the same wire type (`u64`) across all consumers:","-  - `CheckpointState.created_at: u64` — unchanged type, new unit (millis)","-  - `CheckpointFileHeader.created_at: u64` — same","-  - `CheckpointInfo.created_at: u64` — same","-  - `query_router/src/lib.rs` (line 463) — `QueryResult` checkpoint rows already use `u64`, no change needed","-  - `neumann_server/proto/neumann.proto` (line 440) — protobuf `uint64` stays as-is","-  - `neumann_server/src/convert.rs` (line 479) — conversion stays `u64`, no change","-  - Display formatting: `created_at / 1000` to recover seconds for human-readable display","-  - **Secondary sort key**: Sort by `(created_at DESC, id ASC)` as a deterministic tiebreaker. IDs are UUIDs and are unique. Millisecond resolution makes collisions rare; secondary `id` sort guarantees deterministic results.","-- `CheckpointInfo`: remove `artifact_id` field. Keep `id, name, created_at: u64, size, trigger: Option<String>`.","-- Size comes from filesystem (`body_size` from header or `file_size - 4 - header_len`).","-- Update retention test (retention.rs:124): remove \"order not guaranteed\" comment — nanos + secondary ID sort makes ordering deterministic.","-","-### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/src/lib.rs`","-","-- Replace `blob: Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<BlobStore>>` with `store: Arc<dyn CheckpointStore>`","-- `CheckpointManager::new(store: Arc<dyn CheckpointStore>, config: CheckpointConfig)` — no BlobStore, no tokio mutex","-- All methods become sync: `create()`, `rollback()`, `delete()`, `list()` — drop `async`","-- **Locking policy**: One internal `parking_lot::Mutex<()>` (`op_lock`) serializes ALL state-changing operations: `create()`, `create_auto()`, `rollback()`, `delete()`, and future `compact()`. Only `list()` stays outside (read-only, tolerant of concurrent atomic file creation).","-","-  **Why rollback is serialized**: The current system serializes everything through the outer `tokio::sync::Mutex<CheckpointManager>` (query_router:758). Removing that mutex and leaving `rollback()` unserialized introduces a race: rollback resolves a checkpoint ID → concurrent `delete()` removes that file → rollback fails mid-read or loads stale data. Additionally, `rollback()` mutates `TensorStore` state, so two concurrent rollbacks would corrupt data. Keeping it under `op_lock` preserves the current serialization guarantee with no behavior change.","-- `set_confirmation_handler()`: use `RwLock<Option<Arc<dyn ConfirmationHandler>>>` inside `CheckpointManager` so it can be set through `&self` (no `&mut self` needed, compatible with `Arc<CheckpointManager>`)","-","-### Remove: `tensor_checkpoint/src/storage.rs`","-","-Delete entirely. The `BlobCheckpointStore` adapter cannot compile in this crate without `tensor_blob`. If a blob-backed checkpoint backend is needed later, it belongs in a separate crate (e.g., `tensor_checkpoint_blob`) that depends on both `tensor_checkpoint` and `tensor_blob`. No current consumer needs it — all paths migrate to `FileCheckpointStore`.","-","-### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/src/retention.rs`","-","-- `enforce()` takes `&dyn CheckpointStore` → uses `store.list()` + `store.delete()`","-","-### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/Cargo.toml`","-","-- Remove `tensor_blob` dependency","-- Remove `tokio` dependency (no async needed)","-- Add `parking_lot` for internal mutex","-","-### Modify: `query_router/src/lib.rs`","-","-**Complete call site migration (7 sites):**","-","-| Line | Current | After |","-|------|---------|-------|","-| 759 | `checkpoint: Option<Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<CheckpointManager>>>` | `checkpoint: Option<Arc<CheckpointManager>>` |","-| 2957 `exec_checkpoint()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.create(...).await })` | `checkpoint.create(...)` |","-| 2982 `exec_rollback()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.rollback(...).await })` | `checkpoint.rollback(...)` |","-| 3003 `exec_checkpoints()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.list(...).await })` | `checkpoint.list(...)` |","-| 1352 `set_confirmation_handler()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.set_confirmation_handler(h) })` | `checkpoint.set_confirmation_handler(h)` — but needs `&mut self` or internal `RwLock` for handler |","-| 4937 `protect_destructive_op()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.create_auto(...).await })` | `checkpoint.create_auto(...)` |","-| 1269+ `init_checkpoint()` | Creates `CheckpointManager::new(blob_arc, config)` requiring blob store | `CheckpointManager::new(file_store_arc, config)` — no blob dependency |","-","-- **Checkpoint directory — mandatory, no fallback**: Add `checkpoint_dir: Option<PathBuf>` field to `QueryRouter` (next to `checkpoint` at line 759). This field is set once by the caller who knows where persistent data belongs.","-","-  New accessor + setter:","-  ```rust","-  pub fn set_checkpoint_dir(&mut self, dir: PathBuf) { self.checkpoint_dir = Some(dir); }","-  pub fn checkpoint_dir(&self) -> Option<&Path> { self.checkpoint_dir.as_deref() }","-  ```","-","-  **All entry points must wire this before checkpoint operations:**","-","-  | Entry Point | Source of Path | Where Wired |","-  |-------------|---------------|-------------|","-  | **Server (cluster mode)** | `ClusterConfig.data_dir` (config.rs:143) | `main.rs:37` — after `init_cluster_with_wal()`, add `router.write().set_checkpoint_dir(cluster_config.data_dir.join(\"checkpoints\"))` |","-  | **Server (standalone mode)** | New field `ServerConfig.data_dir: Option<PathBuf>` sourced from `NEUMANN_DATA_DIR` env var (config.rs:193). If `None` AND no cluster config, checkpoint is unavailable (no silent fallback). | `main.rs:28` — `if let Some(ref dir) = config.data_dir { router.write().set_checkpoint_dir(dir.join(\"checkpoints\")); }` |","-  | **Shell** | New field `ShellConfig.checkpoint_dir: Option<PathBuf>` with default `dirs_home().map(\\|h\\| h.join(\".neumann\").join(\"checkpoints\"))` (lib.rs:39). Uses same `~/.neumann/` convention as `history_file` uses `~/.neumann_history`. | Set on shell startup: `router.set_checkpoint_dir(config.checkpoint_dir)` |","-  | **Tests** | `tempdir.path().to_path_buf()` | Each test calls `router.set_checkpoint_dir(tempdir.path().to_path_buf())` |","-","-  **Modify: `neumann_server/src/config.rs` (line 193)**","-  - Add to `ServerConfig`: `pub data_dir: Option<PathBuf>` (after existing fields, line ~238)","-  - In `ServerConfig::from_env()` or `Default`: read `NEUMANN_DATA_DIR` env var, map to `PathBuf`. Same env var `ClusterConfig` uses for `data_dir` (line 143).","-  - Default: `None` — standalone server without `NEUMANN_DATA_DIR` simply has no checkpoints, which is the current behavior.","-","-  **Modify: `neumann_shell/src/lib.rs` (lines 39, 137, 148)**","-  - Add to `ShellConfig` (line 39): `pub checkpoint_dir: Option<PathBuf>`","-  - Default (line 58): `dirs_home().map(|h| h.join(\".neumann\").join(\"checkpoints\"))`","-  - **Both constructors** must wire the checkpoint dir into the router they create:","-","-    `Shell::new()` (line 137):","-    ```rust","-    pub fn new() -> Self {","-        let config = ShellConfig::default();","-        let mut router = QueryRouter::new();","-        if let Some(ref dir) = config.checkpoint_dir {","-            router.set_checkpoint_dir(dir.clone());","-        }","-        Self {","-            router: Arc::new(RwLock::new(router)),","-            config,","-            wal: Mutex::new(None),","-            icons: Icons::auto(),","-        }","-    }","-    ```","-","-    `Shell::with_config()` (line 148):","-    ```rust","-    pub fn with_config(mut config: ShellConfig) -> Self {","-        // ... existing no_color logic ...","-        let mut router = QueryRouter::new();","-        if let Some(ref dir) = config.checkpoint_dir {","-            router.set_checkpoint_dir(dir.clone());","-        }","-        Self {","-            router: Arc::new(RwLock::new(router)),","-            config,","-            wal: Mutex::new(None),","-            icons,","-        }","-    }","-    ```","-","-- **`init_checkpoint_with_config()` signature change**: Now takes only `CheckpointConfig` (no `PathBuf` parameter) but reads `self.checkpoint_dir`. Returns `Err` if `checkpoint_dir` is `None`:","-  ```rust","-  pub fn init_checkpoint_with_config(&mut self, config: CheckpointConfig) -> Result<()> {","-      let dir = self.checkpoint_dir.as_ref()","-          .ok_or_else(|| anyhow!(\"checkpoint_dir must be set before initializing checkpoints\"))?;","-      let store = Arc::new(FileCheckpointStore::new(dir)?);","-      self.checkpoint = Some(Arc::new(CheckpointManager::new(store, config)));","-      Ok(())","-  }","-  ```","-  `init_checkpoint()` delegates to `init_checkpoint_with_config(CheckpointConfig::default())` as before.","-","-- **`ensure_checkpoint()`**: Same — reads `self.checkpoint_dir`, returns `Err` if `None`. No temp dir fallback, no silent degradation.","-","-- **No temp dir fallback anywhere**: Production code never guesses a checkpoint location. Tests explicitly set `checkpoint_dir` via `set_checkpoint_dir(tempdir.path())`. If checkpoint_dir is not set, checkpoint operations fail loudly.","-","-- `blob_runtime` remains for BlobStore operations — NOT removed globally","-","-### Modify: `neumann_shell/src/doctor/wal.rs` (line 27-31)","-","-Current: `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.list(Some(1)).await })`","-After: `checkpoint.list(Some(1))` — direct sync call, no runtime needed.","-- `ctx.router.runtime()` check for checkpoint removed (may still be needed for other diagnostics)","-","-### Modify: `neumann_server/src/web/handlers/checkpoint.rs` (lines 19, 31, 92, 105)","-","-Sync file I/O must NOT block async Axum worker threads. Wrap checkpoint calls in `tokio::task::spawn_blocking()`:","-","-```rust","-pub async fn list_view(State(ctx): State<Arc<AdminContext>>) -> Markup {","-    let checkpoint = ctx.checkpoint.clone();","-    let checkpoints = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || {","-        checkpoint.as_ref().map(|cp| cp.list(Some(50)))","-    }).await.unwrap();","-    // ... render","-}","+```bash","+gh pr merge 43 --repo Shadylukin/Neumann --squash --delete-branch"," ```"," ","-Same pattern for `detail_view()` (line 92) which calls `checkpoint.list(Some(100))`.","-- Handler signatures remain `async fn` (axum requirement)","-- `spawn_blocking` moves the filesystem I/O to a dedicated thread pool","-","-### Modify: `neumann_server/src/main.rs` (lines 28-43)","-","-Wire `checkpoint_dir` for both startup modes:","-```rust","-// Standalone: use ServerConfig.data_dir if set","-if let Some(ref dir) = config.data_dir {","-    router.write().set_checkpoint_dir(dir.join(\"checkpoints\"));","-}","-","-// Cluster: override with ClusterConfig.data_dir (always present)","-if let Some(ref cluster_config) = config.cluster {","-    router.write().set_checkpoint_dir(cluster_config.data_dir.join(\"checkpoints\"));","-    // ... existing init_cluster_with_wal() ...","-}","-```","-Cluster config takes precedence over standalone `data_dir` if both are set.","-","-### Modify: `neumann_server/src/web/mod.rs` (line 115)","-","-`pub checkpoint: Option<Arc<CheckpointManager>>` — already correct type (no tokio::sync::Mutex wrapper needed since methods are sync, internal state protected by internal parking_lot locks)","-","-### Modify: `neumann_server/src/web/handlers/checkpoint.rs` (line 150-154)","-","-Remove \"Artifact ID\" display from detail view. Replace with checkpoint `id` which is already shown. The `artifact_id` was a BlobStore implementation detail that no longer exists.","-","-### Modify: `query_router/src/lib.rs` (line 1258)","-","-`checkpoint()` accessor: change return type from `Option<&Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<CheckpointManager>>>` to `Option<&Arc<CheckpointManager>>`.","-","-### Rewrite: `tensor_checkpoint/src/lib.rs` unit tests (line 350+)","-","-All 20 unit tests are currently `#[tokio::test] async fn` with `.await` calls. Convert to `#[test] fn` with sync method calls. Replace `setup().await` with sync `setup()` that creates `FileCheckpointStore::new(tempdir)`.","-","-### Rewrite: `integration_tests/tests/checkpoint.rs` (all 5+ tests)","-","-Currently:","-- Imports `tensor_blob::{BlobConfig, BlobStore}`, `tokio::sync::Mutex`","-- Uses `#[tokio::test]`, `BlobStore::new(store.clone(), ...).await`, `manager.create(...).await`","-","-Replace with:","-- Import `tensor_checkpoint::FileCheckpointStore`","-- Use `#[test]`, `FileCheckpointStore::new(tempdir.path())`, `manager.create(...)`","-- Remove `tensor_blob` dependency from these tests","-","-### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/benches/checkpoint_bench.rs`","-","-Update bench setup: replace `BlobStore` + async block with `FileCheckpointStore` + sync calls. Remove `tokio::runtime::Runtime` usage.","-","-### Complete Migration Inventory","-","-**A. `CheckpointManager::new(blob, ...)` → `CheckpointManager::new(file_store, config)` (26 sites):**","-","-| File | Lines | Context |","-|------|-------|---------|","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 1291 | `init_checkpoint_with_config()` definition — migrates to `FileCheckpointStore::new(dir)` |","-| `tensor_checkpoint/src/lib.rs` | 345,434,556,570,598 | Unit test setup fn + 4 direct calls |","-| `tensor_checkpoint/benches/checkpoint_bench.rs` | 21 | Benchmark setup |","-| `neumann_server/src/web/handlers/checkpoint.rs` | 272,340 | Handler unit tests |","-| `neumann_server/examples/web_preview.rs` | 547 | `seed_checkpoint()` example |","-| `integration_tests/tests/checkpoint.rs` | 20,41,82,111,139,163,181,199,214,229,270,292,314,336,360 | All 15 test setup blocks |","-| `integration_tests/tests/grand_unification.rs` | 42 | Grand unification test setup |","-","-**B. `init_checkpoint_with_config()` callers (6 test sites) — signature unchanged but now reads `self.checkpoint_dir`, so each test must call `router.set_checkpoint_dir(tempdir)` first:**","-","-| File | Line | Test Function |","-|------|------|---------------|","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 13767 | `test_init_checkpoint_with_config()` |","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15433 | `test_delete_creates_auto_checkpoint()` |","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15472 | `test_delete_cancelled_preserves_data()` |","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15509 | `test_delete_with_auto_checkpoint_disabled()` |","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15533 | `test_drop_table_creates_checkpoint()` |","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15562 | `test_node_delete_creates_checkpoint()` |","-","-**C. `init_checkpoint()` callers (25+ test sites) — delegates to `init_checkpoint_with_config(default)`, so each test must also call `set_checkpoint_dir()` first:**","-","-| File | Lines | Count |","-|------|-------|-------|","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 13747,13758,13783,13804,13822,13840,13864,13908,13941,13956,13984,14018,14058,14084,14134,14145,14171,20979 | 18 tests |","-| `integration_tests/tests/cross_engine_atomicity.rs` | 167 | 1 test |","-| `integration_tests/tests/query_router_engine_paths.rs` | 138,173,190,747 | 4 tests |","-","-**D. `ensure_checkpoint()` callers (2 test sites) — same: requires `set_checkpoint_dir()` first:**","-","-| File | Line | Test Function |","-|------|------|---------------|","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 13775 | `test_ensure_checkpoint_auto_init()` |","-| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 13785 | `test_ensure_checkpoint_already_initialized()` |","-","-**E. `checkpoint()` accessor (line 1258) — return type changes from `Option<&Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<CheckpointManager>>>` to `Option<&Arc<CheckpointManager>>`.**","-","-**F. Test at line 13744 (`test_init_checkpoint_requires_blob`)** — rename to `test_init_checkpoint_requires_dir` and test that calling `init_checkpoint()` without `set_checkpoint_dir()` returns an error.","-","-**G. Documentation files referencing old BlobStore-based API:**","-","-| File | Lines |","-|------|-------|","-| `docs/book/src/api-reference.md` | 1011 |","-| `docs/book/src/reference/api/tensor-checkpoint.md` | 140,143 |","-| `docs/book/src/architecture/tensor-checkpoint.md` | 474,477,518,577 |","-| `docs/book/src/how-to/checkpoint-restore.md` | 37 |","-","-### Tests:","-- `FileCheckpointStore`: store/load/list/delete roundtrip","-- `list()` reads only headers — verify with large snapshot + file seek count","-- `CheckpointFileHeader` preserves full `CheckpointTrigger` and `CheckpointMetadata`","-- Atomic writes: partial write leaves no corrupt `.ncp`","-- 3 checkpoints → snapshot sizes stable (no `_blob` accumulation)","-- Retention through sync trait interface","-- Concurrent create + list (parking_lot mutex serializes creates)","-"," ---"," ","-## Phase 1a: Zstd for In-Memory Snapshot Path","+## Step 4: Merge PR #42 (criterion 0.5 → 0.8)"," ","-**Bug**: `to_bytes()` (slab_router.rs:438) returns raw `bitcode::serialize(&v3)`. No compression, no header. Checkpoint stores uncompressed bytes.","+**Problem**: criterion major version bump. MSRV concern: criterion 0.8 requires Rust 1.86, workspace declares `rust-version = \"1.75\"`."," ","-**Fix**: Align in-memory format with file format — raw header + zstd payload.","+**Analysis**: CI passes (all 16 bench targets compile and run). The criterion API used across all bench files (`criterion_group!`, `criterion_main!`, `bench_function`, `BenchmarkId`, `Throughput`, `black_box`) is unchanged. No MSRV CI job exists — only `toolchain: stable` (1.92+) is tested. The `rust-version = \"1.75\"` is aspirational and not enforced."," ","-**Files:**","-- `tensor_store/src/slab_router.rs`:","-  - `to_bytes()`: serialize `SlabRouterSnapshot` via bitcode → zstd level 3 → prepend raw 20-byte `SnapshotHeader` with `FLAG_COMPRESSED`","-  - `from_bytes()`: check first 4 bytes for `b\"NEUM\"` → parse raw header → decompress → bitcode deserialize. If NOT `b\"NEUM\"` → fallback `bitcode::deserialize::<V3Snapshot>` for old format.","-- `tensor_store/src/snapshot.rs`:","-  - Ensure `SnapshotHeader::{to_raw_bytes, from_raw_bytes}` are `pub`","-  - Refactor `load_v3()` to share header-parsing with `from_bytes()`","+**Fix**: Bump MSRV to match reality, then merge."," ","-**Both file and in-memory paths now share the same binary format.** Old uncompressed bytes (bitcode V3Snapshot, no `b\"NEUM\"` prefix) detected by magic check.","+```bash","+# On the PR branch, bump MSRV","+gh pr checkout 42","+# Edit Cargo.toml line 37: rust-version = \"1.75\" → \"1.86\"","+cargo build --package graph_engine  # verify","+git add Cargo.toml && git commit -m \"Bump rust-version to 1.86 for criterion 0.8 compatibility\"","+git push","+gh pr merge 42 --squash --delete-branch","+```"," ","-**Tests:**","-- Existing roundtrip tests pass","-- Old-format bytes still restore (backward compat)","-- Compressed bytes smaller than uncompressed","-- Full checkpoint path roundtrip","+**Files**: `Cargo.toml` (line 37)"," "," ---"," ","-## Phase 1b: Graph Columnar Compression","+## Step 5: Commit aws-lc-sys fix + push"," ","-**Prerequisite**: Phase 0a + Phase 1a.","+Create a single commit on main with both lockfile updates from Step 1."," ","-**Approach**: Version bump V3→V4 with columnar graph encoding. Both file and in-memory paths share version detection via raw header.","-","-**Files:**","-- `tensor_store/src/graph_tensor.rs`:","-  - `CompressedGraphSnapshot` with columnar delta+varint via `tensor_compress::{compress_ids, decompress_ids}`","-  - `compress() -> CompressedGraphSnapshot` / `decompress() -> GraphTensorSnapshot`","-- `tensor_store/src/slab_router.rs`:","-  - `SlabRouterSnapshotV4` with `graph: CompressedGraphSnapshot`","-  - `to_bytes()` writes V4; `from_bytes()` handles V3 and V4 via header version","-- `tensor_store/src/snapshot.rs`:","-  - `CURRENT_VERSION = 4`","-  - `load()` auto-detects V2/V3/V4","-  - `save_v4()` and `load_v4()` for file path","-","-**Both `load_v*()` (file) and `from_bytes()` (in-memory) handle V3 and V4** through shared version detection on raw header. No asymmetry between paths.","-","-**Tests:**","-- Roundtrip 0, 1, 1K, 10K edges (sequential + non-sequential)","-- V3 files and V3 in-memory bytes still load","-- Edge metadata preserved through cycle","-- Size reduction benchmark","-","----","-","-## Phase 2: Incremental Snapshots","-","-**Prerequisite**: Phases 0a-c, 1a.","-","-### 2a. Change Tracker","-- New: `tensor_store/src/change_tracker.rs`","-- Integrated into `SlabRouter` — record on `put()`, `delete()`, `clear()`","-","-### 2b. Delta Checkpoints","-- `CheckpointType::Full | Delta { base_id }` in `CheckpointState`","-- File store handles both types transparently (header includes type discriminant)","-- `create()`: delta if recent base AND changes <50%","-- `rollback()`: resolve chain","-- `compact()`: auto at chain length 10","-","-### 2c. Dependency-Safe Deletion","-- `delete()`: if base for deltas → compact descendants first, then delete","-- `RetentionManager`: compact chains before purging bases","-","----","-","-## Implementation Order","-","+```bash","+git add Cargo.lock neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock","+git commit -m \"Update aws-lc-rs to 1.16.1 to fix aws-lc-sys CVEs\"","+git push"," ```","-Phase 0a (edge ID fix)              — standalone, small, tensor_store only","-    ↓","-Phase 0b (Arc<ArcSwap> + restore)   — after 0a, spans tensor_store + relational_engine (23 slab() sites)","-    ↓","-Phase 1a (zstd in-memory)           — after 0b (both touch to_bytes/from_bytes)","-    ↓","-Phase 1b (graph columnar V4)        — after 1a"," ","-Phase 0c (CheckpointStore + file)   — independent of 0a/0b, largest, touches 6 crates","-    ↓                                  (tensor_checkpoint, query_router, neumann_server,","-Phase 2a-c (incremental)              neumann_shell, integration_tests, tensor_checkpoint bench)","-```","-","-**0a and 0c can proceed in parallel** (no file overlap). **0b must follow 0a** (both modify `graph_tensor.rs` restore path, and 0b is a multi-crate change spanning `tensor_store` + `relational_engine` — not a small standalone change). **0c is independent** and can run in parallel with the 0a→0b sequence.","-"," ---"," ","-## Non-Goals (Explicit)","-","-- **Engine cache refresh after rollback**: Query-level engines (relational, graph, vector) may hold stale caches after `TensorStore` restore. This is documented as a known limitation per `cross_engine_atomicity.rs:219`. Fixing it requires engine-level invalidation hooks, which is a separate change.","-- **Streaming I/O for large snapshots**: Only implement when stores consistently exceed ~500MB. In-memory path is simpler for current workloads.","-- **Replacing `tensor_compress::format::CompressedSnapshot`**: The flat key-value model doesn't match the typed slab architecture. Utility functions (delta encoding, TT) are used directly at slab level.","-","----","-"," ## Verification"," ","-After each phase:","+After all steps:"," ```bash","-cargo fmt --check","-cargo clippy --package tensor_store -- -D warnings -D clippy::pedantic","-cargo clippy --package tensor_checkpoint -- -D warnings -D clippy::pedantic","-cargo clippy --package query_router -- -D warnings -D clippy::pedantic","-cargo nextest run --package tensor_store","-cargo nextest run --package tensor_checkpoint","-cargo nextest run --package query_router","-cargo nextest run --package neumann_server","-cargo nextest run --package neumann_shell","-cargo nextest run --package integration_tests","-```","+# Security audit","+cargo audit"," ","-Coverage:","-```bash","-cargo llvm-cov --package tensor_store --lib --lcov --output-path /tmp/ts.lcov","-lcov --extract /tmp/ts.lcov '*/tensor_store/src/*' --output-file /tmp/ts_only.lcov","-lcov --summary /tmp/ts_only.lcov","-# Repeat for tensor_checkpoint, query_router","+# Confirm no open alerts","+gh api repos/Shadylukin/Neumann/dependabot/alerts --jq '[.[] | select(.state==\"open\")] | length'","+","+# Confirm no open PRs","+gh pr list --repo Shadylukin/Neumann --state open"," ```"," ","-Acceptance (TensorStore level):","-1. Store with graph (non-sequential edge IDs + metadata), relational table (schema + rows), embeddings (768-dim)","-2. `snapshot_bytes()` → `restore_from_bytes()` → verify exact slab state: IDs, rows, vectors, configs","-3. `store.clone()` → restore on clone → original also sees new state (shared swap cell)","-4. `FileCheckpointStore` → create checkpoint → sizes stable across multiple checkpoints","-5. Rollback via `CheckpointManager` → exact TensorStore state match","-6. Compressed in-memory bytes smaller than old format","+## Execution Order","+","+1. aws-lc-sys lockfile update (Step 1 + 5) — on main, standalone commit","+2. Dismiss alert #26 (Step 2) — API call only","+3. Merge PR #43 tabled (Step 3) — direct merge","+4. Merge PR #42 criterion (Step 4) — requires MSRV edit on PR branch first"]}],"originalFile":"# Plan: Fix State Persistence Correctness + Improve Compression\n\n## Context\n\nAudit of Neumann's snapshot/checkpoint system found correctness bugs in the restore path, a circular dependency where checkpoint blobs pollute the store they snapshot, and unused compression infrastructure. This plan fixes the foundation first, then layers on compression.\n\n**Already working well:**\n- Embeddings use `CompressedEmbedding` (TT >=256-dim, sparse >50% zeros) — `embedding_slab.rs:538`\n- File-based snapshots (`save_v3`/`load_v3`) use bitcode + zstd + typed `SlabRouter::restore()` — `snapshot.rs:285,369`\n- Atomic writes via temp file + rename — `snapshot.rs:326`\n\n**Bugs found:**\n1. `restore_from_bytes()` is lossy — scan+put loses graph/relational/embedding slab state and configs — `lib.rs:1326`\n2. `GraphTensor::restore()` allocates fresh edge IDs, breaking metadata references — `graph_tensor.rs:677,299`\n3. Checkpoint blobs in same TensorStore cause unbounded snapshot growth — `streaming.rs:156`, `slab_router.rs:709`\n4. Checkpoint in-memory path skips zstd — `slab_router.rs:438`\n\n**Restore contract**: `CheckpointManager` guarantees exact `TensorStore` restore. Query-engine cache/schema refresh after rollback is a separate concern and is explicitly **out of scope** for this change.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 0a: GraphTensor Edge ID Preservation\n\n**Bug**: `restore()` calls `add_edge()` → `next_edge_id.fetch_add(1)` (line 299). Edges [0,1,3,5] become [0,1,2,3], breaking `edge:*` metadata keys from `edge_data`.\n\n**File**: `tensor_store/src/graph_tensor.rs`\n- Add `fn add_edge_with_id(&self, edge_id: EdgeId, from, to, edge_type, directed)` — same as `add_edge()` but uses provided ID, no fetch_add\n- Change `restore()` (line 660-696):\n  - Move `next_edge_id.store(snapshot.next_edge_id, ...)` BEFORE edge loop\n  - Replace `add_edge(...)` with `add_edge_with_id(edge.edge_id, ...)`\n\n**Tests:**\n- Roundtrip with non-sequential IDs [0,1,3,5,100] → verify exact IDs preserved\n- Edge metadata under `edge:3` maps to correct edge after restore\n- Graph with deletions → snapshot → restore → full fidelity check\n\n---\n\n## Phase 0b: Arc\\<ArcSwap\\> Router for Faithful Restore\n\n**Bug**: `restore_from_bytes()` creates a new `SlabRouter` via `from_bytes()` (correct) but can't swap it into `Arc<SlabRouter>`. Falls back to `scan(\"\") + put()` which routes `node:*/edge:*/table:*` to metadata only (slab_router.rs:189-198), losing graph CSR, relational columns, embeddings, and slab configs (`dimension`, `capacity`, `strategy`, `segment_size`).\n\n**Why Arc\\<ArcSwap\\>**: `TensorStore` is `Clone` with shared-storage semantics (lib.rs:776). `BlobStore::new(store.clone())` (lib.rs:87, query_router:1034) relies on all clones seeing the same data. `Arc<ArcSwap<SlabRouter>>` ensures all clones share one swap cell — after restore, every clone (including BlobStore's) sees the new router.\n\n**Files:**\n- `tensor_store/Cargo.toml` — Add `arc-swap = \"1\"`\n- `tensor_store/src/lib.rs` (17 `self.router.` call sites):\n  - `router: Arc<SlabRouter>` → `router: Arc<ArcSwap<SlabRouter>>` (line 779)\n  - Constructor: `router: Arc::new(ArcSwap::from_pointee(SlabRouter::new()))`\n  - `Clone`: `Arc<ArcSwap<_>>` is Clone via `Arc::clone` — all clones share the swap cell\n  - **`router(&self) -> &SlabRouter`** (line 1026): Cannot return `&SlabRouter` from a transient ArcSwap guard (guard lifetime is too short). Two consumers exist:\n    - `relational_engine/src/lib.rs:2452` — `self.store.router().relations` borrows `&RelationalSlab` through router\n    - `tensor_store/src/lib.rs:3847` — unit test\n\n    **API redesign**: Replace `router()` with `with_router<F, R>(&self, f: F) -> R where F: FnOnce(&SlabRouter) -> R`. This loads the guard once and passes the reference to the closure, keeping the guard alive for the duration. For `RelationalEngine::slab()`:\n    ```rust\n    // Old: &self.store.router().relations\n    // New: Cannot return &RelationalSlab from closure.\n    ```\n    Since `slab()` returns `&RelationalSlab`, and `RelationalSlab` lives inside the guard, this pattern doesn't work for returning references. **Alternative**: `RelationalEngine` caches an `Arc<SlabRouter>` via `load_full()` and refreshes it on a generation counter or subscription. Or: `RelationalEngine::slab()` callers are changed to accept closures. Or: add a dedicated `TensorStore::with_relational_slab<F, R>(&self, f: F) -> R` accessor.\n\n    **Simplest correct approach**: Add `TensorStore::relational_slab(&self) -> Arc<SlabRouter>` that returns `self.router.load_full()` — caller gets an `Arc<SlabRouter>` they can borrow from for the duration of their operation. `RelationalEngine::slab()` becomes:\n    ```rust\n    fn slab_router(&self) -> Arc<SlabRouter> {\n        self.store.load_router()\n    }\n    // Callers: let router = self.slab_router(); let slab = &router.relations; ...\n    ```\n    This requires updating all `slab()` call sites in `relational_engine` to hold the Arc for the scope of their operation.\n\n  - **Multi-access methods**: Any method performing multiple router accesses must `let router = self.router.load();` once at the top and use `router` throughout. Prevents concurrent restore from mixing old and new state.\n  - `store()` method: returns `self.clone()` — engines hold TensorStore clone sharing the swap cell\n  - **`restore_from_bytes()`**:\n    ```\n    let new_router = SlabRouter::from_bytes(bytes)?;\n    self.router.store(Arc::new(new_router));\n    // Rebuild Bloom filter from new router state\n    if let Some(ref filter) = self.bloom_filter {\n        filter.clear();\n        for key in self.router.load().scan(\"\") {\n            filter.add(&key);\n        }\n    }\n    ```\n    Atomic swap + Bloom rebuild. Without rebuild, Bloom-enabled stores return false negatives for keys that existed before the checkpoint but were not re-inserted after. Remove old scan+put path entirely.\n\n**Callers of `TensorStore::router()`** (2 sites — server/shell `router()` returns QueryRouter, not SlabRouter):\n- `relational_engine/src/lib.rs:2452` — see RelationalEngine migration below\n- `tensor_store/src/lib.rs:3847` — unit test → `let r = store.load_router(); assert_eq!(r.len(), 0);`\n\n### RelationalEngine `slab()` Migration (23 call sites)\n\n**Current**: `fn slab(&self) -> &RelationalSlab` (line 2451) returns `&self.store.router().relations`. With `Arc<ArcSwap<SlabRouter>>`, `router()` can't return `&SlabRouter` (guard lifetime too short).\n\n**Migration strategy**: Change `slab()` to return `Arc<SlabRouter>` via `load_full()`. All 23 call sites insert `.relations` into the chain. Since **every call site uses a temporary borrow** (no stored references, no cross-expression lifetimes), this is a mechanical transformation:\n\n```rust\n// Before:\nfn slab(&self) -> &RelationalSlab { &self.store.router().relations }\nself.slab().table_exists(name)\n\n// After:\nfn slab(&self) -> Arc<SlabRouter> { self.store.load_router() }\nself.slab().relations.table_exists(name)\n```\n\n**Complete call site list** — each `self.slab().foo()` becomes `self.slab().relations.foo()`:\n\n| Line | Method | Expression Pattern |\n|------|--------|--------------------|\n| 2296 | `recover_from_metadata()` | `.table_exists(name)` |\n| 2297 | `recover_from_metadata()` | `.create_table(name, schema)` |\n| 2669 | `create_table()` | `.create_table(name, schema).map_err(...)` |\n| 4748 | `drop_table()` | `.drop_table(table)` |\n| 5299 | `row_count()` | `.row_count(table).map_err(...)` |\n| 5351 | `for_each_row()` | `.scan_for_each(table, &mut \\|...\\|)` |\n| 5999 | `has_columnar_data()` | `.get_schema(table).is_some_and(...)` |\n| 6320 | `select_by_indices()` | `.get_rows_by_indices(table, &indices).ok()?` |\n| 6323 | `select_by_indices()` | `.get_schema(table)?` |\n| 6372 | `apply_condition()` | `.row_count(table).ok()?` |\n| 6378 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |\n| 6392 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |\n| 6405 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |\n| 6418 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |\n| 6431 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |\n| 6444 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_int_column(table, col).ok()?` |\n| 6457 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_float_column(table, col).ok()?` |\n| 6470 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_float_column(table, col).ok()?` |\n| 6483 | `apply_condition()` | `.get_float_column(table, col).ok()?` |\n| 6672 | `rollback()` | `.delete(table, *slab_row_id)` |\n| 6700 | `rollback()` | `.restore_row(table, *slab_row_id, old_values)` |\n| 7023 | `update()` | `.update_row(table, *id, &updates).map_err(...)?` |\n| 7123 | `delete()` | `.delete(table, *id).map_err(...)?` |\n\n**Methods with multiple `self.slab()` calls in the same scope** must hoist the Arc to avoid loading the router twice (consistency + performance):\n- `recover_from_metadata()` (lines 2296-2297): `let slab = self.slab(); slab.relations.table_exists(...); slab.relations.create_table(...);`\n- `select_by_indices()` (lines 6320,6323): `let slab = self.slab(); slab.relations.get_rows_by_indices(...); slab.relations.get_schema(...);`\n- `apply_condition()` (lines 6372-6483): `let slab = self.slab();` once at top, 10 uses of `slab.relations.*`\n\n**No other crate calls `TensorStore::router()` for `SlabRouter` access** — `neumann_server` and `neumann_shell` have their own `router()` methods returning `QueryRouter`.\n\n**Tests:**\n- Full roundtrip: graph edges+metadata, relational tables+data, embeddings → `snapshot_bytes()` → `restore_from_bytes()` → verify ALL slab state\n- Clone contract: `store.clone()` sees restore from original\n- Config preservation: `EmbeddingSlab.dimension`, `CacheRing.capacity/strategy` survive roundtrip\n- Concurrent reads during restore (ArcSwap guarantees no torn state)\n- Bloom filter rebuild: enable Bloom → put keys → snapshot → restore with different keys → verify old keys found (Bloom rebuilt from new router state, no false negatives)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 0c: Decouple Checkpoint Storage — Sync Trait + File Backend\n\n**Bug**: `BlobStore` writes `_blob:*` keys into the same TensorStore being snapshotted. Content-addressed chunks are shared via dedup, making selective exclusion unsafe. Each checkpoint captures prior blobs — unbounded growth.\n\n**Design decisions:**\n- `CheckpointConfig` stays policy-only: retention, auto-checkpoint, confirmation, preview size\n- Filesystem location is backend-specific: `FileCheckpointStore::new(path)` takes `PathBuf` directly\n- `CheckpointInfo` drops `artifact_id` — replace with `storage_id: String` (opaque handle, kept private to backend) or remove entirely if callers only need `id, name, created_at, size, trigger`\n- Trait is sync: file I/O doesn't benefit from async, eliminates tokio runtime dependency for checkpoint paths\n\n### New: `tensor_checkpoint/src/checkpoint_store.rs`\n\n```rust\npub trait CheckpointStore: Send + Sync {\n    fn store(&self, state: &CheckpointState) -> Result<String>;\n    fn load(&self, id_or_name: &str) -> Result<CheckpointState>;\n    fn list(&self) -> Result<Vec<CheckpointInfo>>;\n    fn delete(&self, id_or_name: &str) -> Result<()>;\n}\n```\n\n### New: `tensor_checkpoint/src/file_store.rs`\n\n**File format** — two-part for efficient listing:\n```\n[header_len: u32 LE]\n[header: bitcode(CheckpointFileHeader)]\n[body: bitcode(CheckpointBody)]\n```\n\n`CheckpointFileHeader` (read by `list()`, never reads body):\n```rust\nstruct CheckpointFileHeader {\n    id: String,\n    name: String,\n    created_at: u64,\n    trigger: Option<CheckpointTrigger>,  // full trigger, not just String\n    metadata: CheckpointMetadata,         // relational/graph/vector stats\n    body_size: u64,\n}\n```\n\n`CheckpointBody` (read only by `load()`):\n```rust\nstruct CheckpointBody {\n    store_snapshot: Vec<u8>,\n}\n```\n\nOn `load()`, both header and body are read → reconstructed into `CheckpointState { id, name, created_at, trigger, store_snapshot, metadata }`. The full `CheckpointState` model is unchanged; the split is internal to the file format.\n\n**Directory source**: `FileCheckpointStore::new(dir: impl Into<PathBuf>)` takes an explicit path. The directory comes from `QueryRouter.checkpoint_dir` which must be set before any checkpoint operation (see \"Checkpoint directory — mandatory, no fallback\" below). No fallback to temp dirs or WAL siblings.\n\n**Duplicate name resolution**: When `load(\"name\")` or `delete(\"name\")` matches multiple files by name, resolve to the **newest** by `(created_at DESC, id ASC)`. With `u64` millisecond timestamps, same-millisecond collisions are rare; the secondary `id` sort guarantees deterministic results regardless.\n\nOperations:\n- `store()`: serialize header + body separately, write `[header_len][header][body]` to `{dir}/{id}.ncp` via atomic temp+rename. Create directory if it doesn't exist.\n- `load(id_or_name)`: scan directory headers for matching ID first (exact), then name (newest-first if duplicates). Read full file for match.\n- `list()`: scan `*.ncp` files, read first `4 + header_len` bytes from each → build `CheckpointInfo`. Sort by `created_at` descending (newest first).\n- `delete(id_or_name)`: find matching file (same resolution as `load()`), remove it.\n\n### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/src/state.rs`\n\n- **Timestamp precision**: Keep `created_at` as `u64` but change unit from seconds to **milliseconds**. Update `CheckpointState::new()` (line 31) to use `d.as_millis() as u64` instead of `d.as_secs()`. `u64` millis gives ~584 million years of range — no overflow concern. This eliminates the same-second collision documented in retention tests (retention.rs:124) while keeping the same wire type (`u64`) across all consumers:\n  - `CheckpointState.created_at: u64` — unchanged type, new unit (millis)\n  - `CheckpointFileHeader.created_at: u64` — same\n  - `CheckpointInfo.created_at: u64` — same\n  - `query_router/src/lib.rs` (line 463) — `QueryResult` checkpoint rows already use `u64`, no change needed\n  - `neumann_server/proto/neumann.proto` (line 440) — protobuf `uint64` stays as-is\n  - `neumann_server/src/convert.rs` (line 479) — conversion stays `u64`, no change\n  - Display formatting: `created_at / 1000` to recover seconds for human-readable display\n  - **Secondary sort key**: Sort by `(created_at DESC, id ASC)` as a deterministic tiebreaker. IDs are UUIDs and are unique. Millisecond resolution makes collisions rare; secondary `id` sort guarantees deterministic results.\n- `CheckpointInfo`: remove `artifact_id` field. Keep `id, name, created_at: u64, size, trigger: Option<String>`.\n- Size comes from filesystem (`body_size` from header or `file_size - 4 - header_len`).\n- Update retention test (retention.rs:124): remove \"order not guaranteed\" comment — nanos + secondary ID sort makes ordering deterministic.\n\n### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/src/lib.rs`\n\n- Replace `blob: Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<BlobStore>>` with `store: Arc<dyn CheckpointStore>`\n- `CheckpointManager::new(store: Arc<dyn CheckpointStore>, config: CheckpointConfig)` — no BlobStore, no tokio mutex\n- All methods become sync: `create()`, `rollback()`, `delete()`, `list()` — drop `async`\n- **Locking policy**: One internal `parking_lot::Mutex<()>` (`op_lock`) serializes ALL state-changing operations: `create()`, `create_auto()`, `rollback()`, `delete()`, and future `compact()`. Only `list()` stays outside (read-only, tolerant of concurrent atomic file creation).\n\n  **Why rollback is serialized**: The current system serializes everything through the outer `tokio::sync::Mutex<CheckpointManager>` (query_router:758). Removing that mutex and leaving `rollback()` unserialized introduces a race: rollback resolves a checkpoint ID → concurrent `delete()` removes that file → rollback fails mid-read or loads stale data. Additionally, `rollback()` mutates `TensorStore` state, so two concurrent rollbacks would corrupt data. Keeping it under `op_lock` preserves the current serialization guarantee with no behavior change.\n- `set_confirmation_handler()`: use `RwLock<Option<Arc<dyn ConfirmationHandler>>>` inside `CheckpointManager` so it can be set through `&self` (no `&mut self` needed, compatible with `Arc<CheckpointManager>`)\n\n### Remove: `tensor_checkpoint/src/storage.rs`\n\nDelete entirely. The `BlobCheckpointStore` adapter cannot compile in this crate without `tensor_blob`. If a blob-backed checkpoint backend is needed later, it belongs in a separate crate (e.g., `tensor_checkpoint_blob`) that depends on both `tensor_checkpoint` and `tensor_blob`. No current consumer needs it — all paths migrate to `FileCheckpointStore`.\n\n### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/src/retention.rs`\n\n- `enforce()` takes `&dyn CheckpointStore` → uses `store.list()` + `store.delete()`\n\n### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/Cargo.toml`\n\n- Remove `tensor_blob` dependency\n- Remove `tokio` dependency (no async needed)\n- Add `parking_lot` for internal mutex\n\n### Modify: `query_router/src/lib.rs`\n\n**Complete call site migration (7 sites):**\n\n| Line | Current | After |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| 759 | `checkpoint: Option<Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<CheckpointManager>>>` | `checkpoint: Option<Arc<CheckpointManager>>` |\n| 2957 `exec_checkpoint()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.create(...).await })` | `checkpoint.create(...)` |\n| 2982 `exec_rollback()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.rollback(...).await })` | `checkpoint.rollback(...)` |\n| 3003 `exec_checkpoints()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.list(...).await })` | `checkpoint.list(...)` |\n| 1352 `set_confirmation_handler()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.set_confirmation_handler(h) })` | `checkpoint.set_confirmation_handler(h)` — but needs `&mut self` or internal `RwLock` for handler |\n| 4937 `protect_destructive_op()` | `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.create_auto(...).await })` | `checkpoint.create_auto(...)` |\n| 1269+ `init_checkpoint()` | Creates `CheckpointManager::new(blob_arc, config)` requiring blob store | `CheckpointManager::new(file_store_arc, config)` — no blob dependency |\n\n- **Checkpoint directory — mandatory, no fallback**: Add `checkpoint_dir: Option<PathBuf>` field to `QueryRouter` (next to `checkpoint` at line 759). This field is set once by the caller who knows where persistent data belongs.\n\n  New accessor + setter:\n  ```rust\n  pub fn set_checkpoint_dir(&mut self, dir: PathBuf) { self.checkpoint_dir = Some(dir); }\n  pub fn checkpoint_dir(&self) -> Option<&Path> { self.checkpoint_dir.as_deref() }\n  ```\n\n  **All entry points must wire this before checkpoint operations:**\n\n  | Entry Point | Source of Path | Where Wired |\n  |-------------|---------------|-------------|\n  | **Server (cluster mode)** | `ClusterConfig.data_dir` (config.rs:143) | `main.rs:37` — after `init_cluster_with_wal()`, add `router.write().set_checkpoint_dir(cluster_config.data_dir.join(\"checkpoints\"))` |\n  | **Server (standalone mode)** | New field `ServerConfig.data_dir: Option<PathBuf>` sourced from `NEUMANN_DATA_DIR` env var (config.rs:193). If `None` AND no cluster config, checkpoint is unavailable (no silent fallback). | `main.rs:28` — `if let Some(ref dir) = config.data_dir { router.write().set_checkpoint_dir(dir.join(\"checkpoints\")); }` |\n  | **Shell** | New field `ShellConfig.checkpoint_dir: Option<PathBuf>` with default `dirs_home().map(\\|h\\| h.join(\".neumann\").join(\"checkpoints\"))` (lib.rs:39). Uses same `~/.neumann/` convention as `history_file` uses `~/.neumann_history`. | Set on shell startup: `router.set_checkpoint_dir(config.checkpoint_dir)` |\n  | **Tests** | `tempdir.path().to_path_buf()` | Each test calls `router.set_checkpoint_dir(tempdir.path().to_path_buf())` |\n\n  **Modify: `neumann_server/src/config.rs` (line 193)**\n  - Add to `ServerConfig`: `pub data_dir: Option<PathBuf>` (after existing fields, line ~238)\n  - In `ServerConfig::from_env()` or `Default`: read `NEUMANN_DATA_DIR` env var, map to `PathBuf`. Same env var `ClusterConfig` uses for `data_dir` (line 143).\n  - Default: `None` — standalone server without `NEUMANN_DATA_DIR` simply has no checkpoints, which is the current behavior.\n\n  **Modify: `neumann_shell/src/lib.rs` (lines 39, 137, 148)**\n  - Add to `ShellConfig` (line 39): `pub checkpoint_dir: Option<PathBuf>`\n  - Default (line 58): `dirs_home().map(|h| h.join(\".neumann\").join(\"checkpoints\"))`\n  - **Both constructors** must wire the checkpoint dir into the router they create:\n\n    `Shell::new()` (line 137):\n    ```rust\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\n        let config = ShellConfig::default();\n        let mut router = QueryRouter::new();\n        if let Some(ref dir) = config.checkpoint_dir {\n            router.set_checkpoint_dir(dir.clone());\n        }\n        Self {\n            router: Arc::new(RwLock::new(router)),\n            config,\n            wal: Mutex::new(None),\n            icons: Icons::auto(),\n        }\n    }\n    ```\n\n    `Shell::with_config()` (line 148):\n    ```rust\n    pub fn with_config(mut config: ShellConfig) -> Self {\n        // ... existing no_color logic ...\n        let mut router = QueryRouter::new();\n        if let Some(ref dir) = config.checkpoint_dir {\n            router.set_checkpoint_dir(dir.clone());\n        }\n        Self {\n            router: Arc::new(RwLock::new(router)),\n            config,\n            wal: Mutex::new(None),\n            icons,\n        }\n    }\n    ```\n\n- **`init_checkpoint_with_config()` signature change**: Now takes only `CheckpointConfig` (no `PathBuf` parameter) but reads `self.checkpoint_dir`. Returns `Err` if `checkpoint_dir` is `None`:\n  ```rust\n  pub fn init_checkpoint_with_config(&mut self, config: CheckpointConfig) -> Result<()> {\n      let dir = self.checkpoint_dir.as_ref()\n          .ok_or_else(|| anyhow!(\"checkpoint_dir must be set before initializing checkpoints\"))?;\n      let store = Arc::new(FileCheckpointStore::new(dir)?);\n      self.checkpoint = Some(Arc::new(CheckpointManager::new(store, config)));\n      Ok(())\n  }\n  ```\n  `init_checkpoint()` delegates to `init_checkpoint_with_config(CheckpointConfig::default())` as before.\n\n- **`ensure_checkpoint()`**: Same — reads `self.checkpoint_dir`, returns `Err` if `None`. No temp dir fallback, no silent degradation.\n\n- **No temp dir fallback anywhere**: Production code never guesses a checkpoint location. Tests explicitly set `checkpoint_dir` via `set_checkpoint_dir(tempdir.path())`. If checkpoint_dir is not set, checkpoint operations fail loudly.\n\n- `blob_runtime` remains for BlobStore operations — NOT removed globally\n\n### Modify: `neumann_shell/src/doctor/wal.rs` (line 27-31)\n\nCurrent: `runtime.block_on(async { checkpoint.lock().await.list(Some(1)).await })`\nAfter: `checkpoint.list(Some(1))` — direct sync call, no runtime needed.\n- `ctx.router.runtime()` check for checkpoint removed (may still be needed for other diagnostics)\n\n### Modify: `neumann_server/src/web/handlers/checkpoint.rs` (lines 19, 31, 92, 105)\n\nSync file I/O must NOT block async Axum worker threads. Wrap checkpoint calls in `tokio::task::spawn_blocking()`:\n\n```rust\npub async fn list_view(State(ctx): State<Arc<AdminContext>>) -> Markup {\n    let checkpoint = ctx.checkpoint.clone();\n    let checkpoints = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || {\n        checkpoint.as_ref().map(|cp| cp.list(Some(50)))\n    }).await.unwrap();\n    // ... render\n}\n```\n\nSame pattern for `detail_view()` (line 92) which calls `checkpoint.list(Some(100))`.\n- Handler signatures remain `async fn` (axum requirement)\n- `spawn_blocking` moves the filesystem I/O to a dedicated thread pool\n\n### Modify: `neumann_server/src/main.rs` (lines 28-43)\n\nWire `checkpoint_dir` for both startup modes:\n```rust\n// Standalone: use ServerConfig.data_dir if set\nif let Some(ref dir) = config.data_dir {\n    router.write().set_checkpoint_dir(dir.join(\"checkpoints\"));\n}\n\n// Cluster: override with ClusterConfig.data_dir (always present)\nif let Some(ref cluster_config) = config.cluster {\n    router.write().set_checkpoint_dir(cluster_config.data_dir.join(\"checkpoints\"));\n    // ... existing init_cluster_with_wal() ...\n}\n```\nCluster config takes precedence over standalone `data_dir` if both are set.\n\n### Modify: `neumann_server/src/web/mod.rs` (line 115)\n\n`pub checkpoint: Option<Arc<CheckpointManager>>` — already correct type (no tokio::sync::Mutex wrapper needed since methods are sync, internal state protected by internal parking_lot locks)\n\n### Modify: `neumann_server/src/web/handlers/checkpoint.rs` (line 150-154)\n\nRemove \"Artifact ID\" display from detail view. Replace with checkpoint `id` which is already shown. The `artifact_id` was a BlobStore implementation detail that no longer exists.\n\n### Modify: `query_router/src/lib.rs` (line 1258)\n\n`checkpoint()` accessor: change return type from `Option<&Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<CheckpointManager>>>` to `Option<&Arc<CheckpointManager>>`.\n\n### Rewrite: `tensor_checkpoint/src/lib.rs` unit tests (line 350+)\n\nAll 20 unit tests are currently `#[tokio::test] async fn` with `.await` calls. Convert to `#[test] fn` with sync method calls. Replace `setup().await` with sync `setup()` that creates `FileCheckpointStore::new(tempdir)`.\n\n### Rewrite: `integration_tests/tests/checkpoint.rs` (all 5+ tests)\n\nCurrently:\n- Imports `tensor_blob::{BlobConfig, BlobStore}`, `tokio::sync::Mutex`\n- Uses `#[tokio::test]`, `BlobStore::new(store.clone(), ...).await`, `manager.create(...).await`\n\nReplace with:\n- Import `tensor_checkpoint::FileCheckpointStore`\n- Use `#[test]`, `FileCheckpointStore::new(tempdir.path())`, `manager.create(...)`\n- Remove `tensor_blob` dependency from these tests\n\n### Modify: `tensor_checkpoint/benches/checkpoint_bench.rs`\n\nUpdate bench setup: replace `BlobStore` + async block with `FileCheckpointStore` + sync calls. Remove `tokio::runtime::Runtime` usage.\n\n### Complete Migration Inventory\n\n**A. `CheckpointManager::new(blob, ...)` → `CheckpointManager::new(file_store, config)` (26 sites):**\n\n| File | Lines | Context |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 1291 | `init_checkpoint_with_config()` definition — migrates to `FileCheckpointStore::new(dir)` |\n| `tensor_checkpoint/src/lib.rs` | 345,434,556,570,598 | Unit test setup fn + 4 direct calls |\n| `tensor_checkpoint/benches/checkpoint_bench.rs` | 21 | Benchmark setup |\n| `neumann_server/src/web/handlers/checkpoint.rs` | 272,340 | Handler unit tests |\n| `neumann_server/examples/web_preview.rs` | 547 | `seed_checkpoint()` example |\n| `integration_tests/tests/checkpoint.rs` | 20,41,82,111,139,163,181,199,214,229,270,292,314,336,360 | All 15 test setup blocks |\n| `integration_tests/tests/grand_unification.rs` | 42 | Grand unification test setup |\n\n**B. `init_checkpoint_with_config()` callers (6 test sites) — signature unchanged but now reads `self.checkpoint_dir`, so each test must call `router.set_checkpoint_dir(tempdir)` first:**\n\n| File | Line | Test Function |\n|------|------|---------------|\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 13767 | `test_init_checkpoint_with_config()` |\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15433 | `test_delete_creates_auto_checkpoint()` |\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15472 | `test_delete_cancelled_preserves_data()` |\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15509 | `test_delete_with_auto_checkpoint_disabled()` |\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15533 | `test_drop_table_creates_checkpoint()` |\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 15562 | `test_node_delete_creates_checkpoint()` |\n\n**C. `init_checkpoint()` callers (25+ test sites) — delegates to `init_checkpoint_with_config(default)`, so each test must also call `set_checkpoint_dir()` first:**\n\n| File | Lines | Count |\n|------|-------|-------|\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 13747,13758,13783,13804,13822,13840,13864,13908,13941,13956,13984,14018,14058,14084,14134,14145,14171,20979 | 18 tests |\n| `integration_tests/tests/cross_engine_atomicity.rs` | 167 | 1 test |\n| `integration_tests/tests/query_router_engine_paths.rs` | 138,173,190,747 | 4 tests |\n\n**D. `ensure_checkpoint()` callers (2 test sites) — same: requires `set_checkpoint_dir()` first:**\n\n| File | Line | Test Function |\n|------|------|---------------|\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 13775 | `test_ensure_checkpoint_auto_init()` |\n| `query_router/src/lib.rs` | 13785 | `test_ensure_checkpoint_already_initialized()` |\n\n**E. `checkpoint()` accessor (line 1258) — return type changes from `Option<&Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<CheckpointManager>>>` to `Option<&Arc<CheckpointManager>>`.**\n\n**F. Test at line 13744 (`test_init_checkpoint_requires_blob`)** — rename to `test_init_checkpoint_requires_dir` and test that calling `init_checkpoint()` without `set_checkpoint_dir()` returns an error.\n\n**G. Documentation files referencing old BlobStore-based API:**\n\n| File | Lines |\n|------|-------|\n| `docs/book/src/api-reference.md` | 1011 |\n| `docs/book/src/reference/api/tensor-checkpoint.md` | 140,143 |\n| `docs/book/src/architecture/tensor-checkpoint.md` | 474,477,518,577 |\n| `docs/book/src/how-to/checkpoint-restore.md` | 37 |\n\n### Tests:\n- `FileCheckpointStore`: store/load/list/delete roundtrip\n- `list()` reads only headers — verify with large snapshot + file seek count\n- `CheckpointFileHeader` preserves full `CheckpointTrigger` and `CheckpointMetadata`\n- Atomic writes: partial write leaves no corrupt `.ncp`\n- 3 checkpoints → snapshot sizes stable (no `_blob` accumulation)\n- Retention through sync trait interface\n- Concurrent create + list (parking_lot mutex serializes creates)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1a: Zstd for In-Memory Snapshot Path\n\n**Bug**: `to_bytes()` (slab_router.rs:438) returns raw `bitcode::serialize(&v3)`. No compression, no header. Checkpoint stores uncompressed bytes.\n\n**Fix**: Align in-memory format with file format — raw header + zstd payload.\n\n**Files:**\n- `tensor_store/src/slab_router.rs`:\n  - `to_bytes()`: serialize `SlabRouterSnapshot` via bitcode → zstd level 3 → prepend raw 20-byte `SnapshotHeader` with `FLAG_COMPRESSED`\n  - `from_bytes()`: check first 4 bytes for `b\"NEUM\"` → parse raw header → decompress → bitcode deserialize. If NOT `b\"NEUM\"` → fallback `bitcode::deserialize::<V3Snapshot>` for old format.\n- `tensor_store/src/snapshot.rs`:\n  - Ensure `SnapshotHeader::{to_raw_bytes, from_raw_bytes}` are `pub`\n  - Refactor `load_v3()` to share header-parsing with `from_bytes()`\n\n**Both file and in-memory paths now share the same binary format.** Old uncompressed bytes (bitcode V3Snapshot, no `b\"NEUM\"` prefix) detected by magic check.\n\n**Tests:**\n- Existing roundtrip tests pass\n- Old-format bytes still restore (backward compat)\n- Compressed bytes smaller than uncompressed\n- Full checkpoint path roundtrip\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1b: Graph Columnar Compression\n\n**Prerequisite**: Phase 0a + Phase 1a.\n\n**Approach**: Version bump V3→V4 with columnar graph encoding. Both file and in-memory paths share version detection via raw header.\n\n**Files:**\n- `tensor_store/src/graph_tensor.rs`:\n  - `CompressedGraphSnapshot` with columnar delta+varint via `tensor_compress::{compress_ids, decompress_ids}`\n  - `compress() -> CompressedGraphSnapshot` / `decompress() -> GraphTensorSnapshot`\n- `tensor_store/src/slab_router.rs`:\n  - `SlabRouterSnapshotV4` with `graph: CompressedGraphSnapshot`\n  - `to_bytes()` writes V4; `from_bytes()` handles V3 and V4 via header version\n- `tensor_store/src/snapshot.rs`:\n  - `CURRENT_VERSION = 4`\n  - `load()` auto-detects V2/V3/V4\n  - `save_v4()` and `load_v4()` for file path\n\n**Both `load_v*()` (file) and `from_bytes()` (in-memory) handle V3 and V4** through shared version detection on raw header. No asymmetry between paths.\n\n**Tests:**\n- Roundtrip 0, 1, 1K, 10K edges (sequential + non-sequential)\n- V3 files and V3 in-memory bytes still load\n- Edge metadata preserved through cycle\n- Size reduction benchmark\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Incremental Snapshots\n\n**Prerequisite**: Phases 0a-c, 1a.\n\n### 2a. Change Tracker\n- New: `tensor_store/src/change_tracker.rs`\n- Integrated into `SlabRouter` — record on `put()`, `delete()`, `clear()`\n\n### 2b. Delta Checkpoints\n- `CheckpointType::Full | Delta { base_id }` in `CheckpointState`\n- File store handles both types transparently (header includes type discriminant)\n- `create()`: delta if recent base AND changes <50%\n- `rollback()`: resolve chain\n- `compact()`: auto at chain length 10\n\n### 2c. Dependency-Safe Deletion\n- `delete()`: if base for deltas → compact descendants first, then delete\n- `RetentionManager`: compact chains before purging bases\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n```\nPhase 0a (edge ID fix)              — standalone, small, tensor_store only\n    ↓\nPhase 0b (Arc<ArcSwap> + restore)   — after 0a, spans tensor_store + relational_engine (23 slab() sites)\n    ↓\nPhase 1a (zstd in-memory)           — after 0b (both touch to_bytes/from_bytes)\n    ↓\nPhase 1b (graph columnar V4)        — after 1a\n\nPhase 0c (CheckpointStore + file)   — independent of 0a/0b, largest, touches 6 crates\n    ↓                                  (tensor_checkpoint, query_router, neumann_server,\nPhase 2a-c (incremental)              neumann_shell, integration_tests, tensor_checkpoint bench)\n```\n\n**0a and 0c can proceed in parallel** (no file overlap). **0b must follow 0a** (both modify `graph_tensor.rs` restore path, and 0b is a multi-crate change spanning `tensor_store` + `relational_engine` — not a small standalone change). **0c is independent** and can run in parallel with the 0a→0b sequence.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Goals (Explicit)\n\n- **Engine cache refresh after rollback**: Query-level engines (relational, graph, vector) may hold stale caches after `TensorStore` restore. This is documented as a known limitation per `cross_engine_atomicity.rs:219`. Fixing it requires engine-level invalidation hooks, which is a separate change.\n- **Streaming I/O for large snapshots**: Only implement when stores consistently exceed ~500MB. In-memory path is simpler for current workloads.\n- **Replacing `tensor_compress::format::CompressedSnapshot`**: The flat key-value model doesn't match the typed slab architecture. Utility functions (delta encoding, TT) are used directly at slab level.\n\n---\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter each phase:\n```bash\ncargo fmt --check\ncargo clippy --package tensor_store -- -D warnings -D clippy::pedantic\ncargo clippy --package tensor_checkpoint -- -D warnings -D clippy::pedantic\ncargo clippy --package query_router -- -D warnings -D clippy::pedantic\ncargo nextest run --package tensor_store\ncargo nextest run --package tensor_checkpoint\ncargo nextest run --package query_router\ncargo nextest run --package neumann_server\ncargo nextest run --package neumann_shell\ncargo nextest run --package integration_tests\n```\n\nCoverage:\n```bash\ncargo llvm-cov --package tensor_store --lib --lcov --output-path /tmp/ts.lcov\nlcov --extract /tmp/ts.lcov '*/tensor_store/src/*' --output-file /tmp/ts_only.lcov\nlcov --summary /tmp/ts_only.lcov\n# Repeat for tensor_checkpoint, query_router\n```\n\nAcceptance (TensorStore level):\n1. Store with graph (non-sequential edge IDs + metadata), relational table (schema + rows), embeddings (768-dim)\n2. `snapshot_bytes()` → `restore_from_bytes()` → verify exact slab state: IDs, rows, vectors, configs\n3. `store.clone()` → restore on clone → original also sees new state (shared swap cell)\n4. `FileCheckpointStore` → create checkpoint → sizes stable across multiple checkpoints\n5. Rollback via `CheckpointManager` → exact TensorStore state match\n6. Compressed in-memory bytes smaller than old format\n"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6986df17-cb58-4ced-83ae-77dfad3afaa2"}
