{"parentUuid":"ecbe1f0c-d499-4a0a-904d-d26e7acc8ff9","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The session covers three phases of work:\n   \n   **Phase 1 (COMPLETE)**: Fix 3 CI failures on PR #65 (`publish-and-snapshot-improvements`):\n   - Benchmark PR failure (`--benches` flag including lib targets)\n   - Fuzz `consensus_conflict` crash (sparse_vector dimension mismatch panic)\n   - Fuzz Summary (dependent on consensus_conflict)\n   \n   **Phase 2 (COMPLETE)**: Merge PR #65 and review/merge all open Dependabot PRs:\n   - Merged 10 PRs (#65, #66, #64, #55, #53, #54, #56, #58, #59, #57)\n   - Closed 3 PRs (#40 outdated, #41 incompatible, #50 superseded)\n   - 2 PRs remain: #42 (criterion 0.5→0.8), #43 (tabled 0.17→0.20)\n   \n   **Phase 3 (IN PROGRESS)**: Plan mode to clear remaining PRs #42/#43 and fix 6 Dependabot security alerts:\n   - aws-lc-sys CVEs (alerts #19-24): PKCS7_verify bypass x2, AES-CCM timing side-channel\n   - minimatch ReDoS (alert #26): false positive in neumann-ts\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - `cargo bench --benches` includes lib targets (built-in harness), `--bench '*'` selects only `[[bench]]` targets\n   - `debug_assert_eq!` panics in debug builds (fuzz runs debug mode) — replaced with graceful early returns for dimension mismatches\n   - Benchmark state accumulation: shared `QueryRouter` across bench groups causes exponential growth\n   - CI workflow scope: `bench-pr.yml` only triggers on `src/**` or `**/benches/**` path changes, NOT root `Cargo.toml` changes\n   - Workspace exclusions (`Cargo.toml:25`): `fuzz`, `neumann-py/neumann-native`, `experiments`, `seed_model`, `demos/knowledge-galaxy` are excluded from `cargo --workspace` commands\n   - `rust-version` (MSRV) in workspace Cargo.toml is inherited by published crates — criterion is a dev-dependency only so doesn't affect published MSRV\n   - aws-lc-sys dependency chain: `tonic → rustls → aws-lc-rs → aws-lc-sys`\n   - `cargo update -p aws-lc-rs` bumps aws-lc-rs 1.16.0→1.16.1 which pulls aws-lc-sys 0.38.0 (patched)\n   - Package name vs directory name: `neumann_shell/` directory has package name `neumann` (renamed in this branch, still old name on main)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`.github/workflows/bench-pr.yml`** — Benchmark PR workflow, heavily modified across 4 commits:\n     - Changed `--benches` to `--bench '*'` (selects only `[[bench]]` targets)\n     - Added crate detection via `git diff` to only benchmark changed crates\n     - Added `fetch-depth: 0` for git diff\n     - Increased timeout 45→90 minutes\n     - Resolved package names from each branch's own Cargo.toml (handles rename)\n     - Added shellcheck disable for intentional word splitting\n     - Key sections: detect step outputs directory names, each bench step resolves via `sed -n 's/^name = \"\\(.*\\)\"/\\1/p'`\n\n   - **`tensor_store/src/sparse_vector.rs`** — Fixed dimension mismatch panics:\n     - `dot_f64()` (line ~420): `debug_assert_eq!` → early return 0.0\n     - `dot_dense()` (line ~451): `debug_assert_eq!` → early return 0.0\n     - `weighted_jaccard()` (line ~889): `debug_assert_eq!` → early return 0.0\n     - `euclidean_distance_squared_f64()` (line ~967): `debug_assert_eq!` → early return `f64::INFINITY`\n     - `manhattan_distance()` (line ~1016): `debug_assert_eq!` → early return `f32::INFINITY`\n     - Added 6 tests at end of test module (lines ~1900+):\n       ```rust\n       #[test]\n       fn dot_dimension_mismatch_returns_zero() {\n           let a = SparseVector::from_dense(&[1.0, 2.0, 3.0]);\n           let b = SparseVector::from_dense(&[1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0]);\n           assert_eq!(a.dot(&b), 0.0);\n       }\n       ```\n       (plus tests for dot_dense, cosine_similarity, weighted_jaccard, euclidean_distance, manhattan_distance)\n\n   - **`query_router/benches/query_router_bench.rs`** — Fixed find_node benchmark timeout:\n     ```rust\n     // Use a dedicated router so find_node isn't affected by accumulated\n     // nodes from the node_create benchmark above.\n     let find_router = QueryRouter::new();\n     for i in 0..100 {\n         find_router\n             .execute_parsed(&format!(\n                 \"NODE CREATE person {{id: {}, name: 'person{}'}}\",\n                 i, i\n             ))\n             .unwrap();\n     }\n     group.sample_size(10);\n     group.bench_function(\"find_node\", |b| {\n         b.iter(|| {\n             let result = find_router\n                 .execute_parsed(black_box(\"FIND NODE WHERE id > 0\"))\n                 .unwrap();\n             black_box(result);\n         });\n     });\n     ```\n\n   - **`fuzz/fuzz_targets/consensus_conflict.rs`** — The fuzz target creating DeltaVectors with variable dimensions (Put=variable len, Delete=4, Embed=variable dim)\n\n   - **`Cargo.toml`** (workspace root) — Key lines:\n     - Line 25: `exclude = [\"fuzz\", \"neumann-py/neumann-native\", \"experiments\", \"seed_model\", \"demos/knowledge-galaxy\"]`\n     - Line 37: `rust-version = \"1.75\"`\n     - Line 98: `criterion = { version = \"0.5\", features = [\"html_reports\"] }`\n\n   - **Lockfiles with aws-lc-sys versions**:\n     - `Cargo.lock`: aws-lc-sys 0.37.1 (VULNERABLE)\n     - `neumann-py/neumann-native/Cargo.lock`: aws-lc-sys 0.37.0 (VULNERABLE)\n     - `fuzz/Cargo.lock`: aws-lc-sys 0.35.0 (VULNERABLE)\n     - `demos/knowledge-galaxy/Cargo.lock`: aws-lc-sys 0.38.0 (PATCHED)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **euclidean_distance test failure**: Asserted `f32::INFINITY` but got `f32::MAX` (3.4028235e38). Root cause: `euclidean_distance()` and `euclidean_distance_squared()` have overflow guards that clamp `f64::INFINITY` to `f32::MAX`. Fixed by changing test assertion to `f32::MAX`.\n   \n   - **Benchmark `--benches` flag**: `cargo bench --benches` includes lib targets whose built-in test harness doesn't understand `--save-baseline`. Fixed by using `--bench '*'` which selects only `[[bench]]` targets.\n   \n   - **find_node benchmark timeout (1707s estimate)**: Shared `QueryRouter` accumulated ~900k nodes from prior `node_create` bench iterations. Fixed with dedicated router + `sample_size(10)`.\n   \n   - **Full workspace benchmark timeout (45min)**: 16 crates × 2 runs (base+PR) exceeded CI timeout. Fixed by detecting changed crates via `git diff` and only benchmarking those.\n   \n   - **Package name mismatch on base branch**: `-p neumann` fails on main where package is still named differently. Fixed by resolving package names from each branch's own Cargo.toml at runtime.\n\n   - **Plan review feedback (3 iterations)**:\n     - Iteration 1: User rejected — MSRV bump was too invasive for a benchmark dep, verification was inadequate, didn't cover all lockfiles\n     - Iteration 2: User rejected — CI evidence overstated (bench-pr workflow doesn't trigger on root Cargo.toml changes), excluded workspaces not separately verified\n     - Iteration 3: User rejected — missing `git push` after commit, final `cargo audit` only covers root workspace, minimatch line references reversed\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **SOLVED**: All 3 original CI failures on PR #65 (benchmark, fuzz, fuzz summary)\n   - **SOLVED**: PR #65 merged successfully\n   - **SOLVED**: 10 Dependabot PRs merged, 3 closed\n   - **IN PROGRESS**: Plan for remaining 2 PRs (#42, #43) and 6 security alerts — plan needs fixes for iteration 4\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"resume\" (after /compact)\n   - \"Yes please\" (commit and push CI fixes)\n   - \"Run Benchmarks cancelled 48 minutes ago in 45m 16s\" (benchmark still timing out, with full CI output showing find_node estimating 1707s)\n   - \"Run Benchmarks failed now in 1m 52s\" (package 'neumann' not found error on base branch)\n   - \"I think this PR is good for merge right?\"\n   - \"Please merge then review the other PR's\"\n   - \"What is left. Do we need to make changes to the code for them? Please enter plan mode to clear remaining PRs and address:\" followed by 7 Dependabot security alerts (aws-lc-sys alerts #19-24, minimatch alert #26)\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch)\n   - Plan rejection 1 (High: MSRV change under-validated and user-visible; Medium: not full repo cleanup; Medium: verification below repo quality gates)\n   - Plan rejection 2 (High: CI evidence overstated for criterion — bench workflow doesn't trigger on root Cargo.toml; Medium: excluded workspaces not verified; Low/confirmed: tabled and minimatch analysis sound)\n   - Plan rejection 3 (Medium: missing git push; Medium: cargo audit only covers root; Low: minimatch line refs reversed)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix plan iteration 4: Add `git push` after lockfile commit, add per-workspace `cargo audit` for excluded workspaces, correct minimatch line references\n   - Execute plan once approved:\n     1. Update aws-lc-sys across all 3 vulnerable lockfiles + push\n     2. Dismiss minimatch alert #26\n     3. Merge PR #43 (tabled 0.17→0.20)\n     4. Merge PR #42 (criterion 0.5→0.8) after local bench compilation check\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Plan mode is active. The plan file at `/Users/lukin/.claude/plans/mighty-hugging-umbrella.md` needs a 4th iteration to address the user's latest feedback:\n   \n   - **Missing git push**: Step 1 commits lockfile changes on main but never pushes to remote. Later steps (alert check, PR merges) operate against remote state.\n   - **Incomplete audit scope**: Final `cargo audit` only audits root workspace. Need separate audit runs in `fuzz/` and `neumann-py/neumann-native/` directories, or explicitly scope the audit as root-only.\n   - **Reversed minimatch references**: `package-lock.json:596` is minimatch 3.1.5, `package-lock.json:2768` is 9.0.9 (currently stated in reverse).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Update the plan file to fix the three issues from the user's latest rejection, then call `ExitPlanMode`. Specifically:\n   \n   - Add `git push` after the commit in Step 1\n   - Add `cd fuzz && cargo audit && cd ..` and `cd neumann-py/neumann-native && cargo audit && cd ../..` to the final verification section (or explicitly scope root audit)\n   - Correct minimatch line references: swap 596↔2768\n   \n   The user's most recent feedback was: \"Medium: Step 1 still does not include a git push after the main-branch commit... Medium: The final security verification is still narrower than the stated goal... Low: The minimatch evidence line references are reversed.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/lukin/.claude/projects/-Users-lukin-Neumann/f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"21134d94-7904-4a8b-bfb5-eed451030565","timestamp":"2026-03-13T01:20:33.714Z"}
